-13 · Launch the slice: one fresh day through the wired path, live, on its own $1.50 ledger (council consensus under D439)\n4984:## D451 · 2026-11-13 · Launch the full run: three clean draws and three production draws, same day, ledger $14.84 (council consensus under D439)\n4999:## D452 · 2026-11-13 · The reading plan for the full run (council consensus under D439)\n5013:## D453 · 2026-11-13 · Redo c2's Step 1 (a dropped response; council consensus under D439)\n5022:## D454 · 2026-11-13 · After the census and Stage A of the full run: the readings continue in the agreed order (council consensus under D439)\n5037:## D455 · 2026-11-13 · Stage B's judgement reading stops for the full run: line 3 is unexercised under every treatment (council consensus under D439)\n5054:## D456 · 2026-11-13 · The next angle: trace production's kept-but-unlinked facts at $0, beside the clean path's (council consensus under D439)\n5070:## D457 · 2026-11-13 · Production's unlinked facts cost no final answer in this window; next a $0 review of the opening losses (council consensus under D439)\n5090:## D458 · 2026-11-13 · No opening phase on the review's evidence; next a $0 trace of Stage A's agreed failures (council consensus under D439)\n5111:## D459 · 2026-11-13 · Stage A's first-pass faults form no class; next the standard's tests on the three unsettled opening classes and a bounded model-account diagnostic (council consensus under D439)\n5130:## D460 · 2026-11-13 · Next a whole-request $0 prompt audit of clean Step 1 (c8), identity first (council consensus under D439)\n5151:## D461 · 2026-11-13 · The prompt audit's result; the date contradiction (F6) is designed and falsified first, the identity lever deferred (council consensus under D439)\n5166:## D462 · 2026-11-13 · F6 is recorded as a contradiction with uncertain standalone effect; the status report for Alex comes before the identity comparison (council consensus under D439)\n5181:## D463 · 2026-11-13 · The identity lever: a general prompt clause first (P), written and probe-designed before any send (council consensus under D439)\n5201:## D464 · 2026-11-13 · Send the case-specific identity diagnostic, c16 version 5 against c8, under one $5 ledger (council consensus under D439)\n5286:## D469 · 2026-11-13 · Provisional choices while Alex has not answered; the ladder-step refusal fix starts with a $0 boundary check (council consensus under D439)\n5297:## D470 · 2026-11-13 · The ladder-refusal candidate stops; the 41 Stage A splits are recorded, eight with a provisional reading from D414; Stage A's verdict is unchanged (council consensus under D439)\n5311:## D471 · 2026-11-13 · The written-ladder line stands; the ten \"right only by refusal\" theses traced; one period-rule candidate (c17) probed on stored cases (council consensus under D439)\n5327:## D472 · 2026-11-13 · A budget exception for the period probe: the nine never-sent jobs are sent before any answer is read (council consensus under D439)\n5336:## D473 · 2026-11-13 · The period candidate c17 fails its frozen lines; Step 1 sentence changes on these articles stop (council consensus under D439)\n5349:## D474 · 2026-11-13 · The unsigned-deal candidate c18 is probed on unseen articles against a stored library (council consensus under D439)\n5372:## D476 · 2026-11-13 · Next test: a $0 source check of the eleven first-pass refusals (council consensus under D439)\n5384:## D477 · 2026-11-13 · Reflection rounds 19–22: Stage A not passed; no H100 or Step 1 change; production stays the default; the clean path's choices go to Alex (council consensus under D439)\n5403:## D478 · 2026-11-13 · Under D439 the council takes D477's choice 2 and probes it: the first step writes each new thesis's settling figure or event and its fixed outcomes (c19)\n5417:## D479 · 2026-11-13 · c19 fails; under D439 the council takes D477's choice 3: production stays the default and the next test comes from production's own losses\n5428:## D480 · 2026-11-13 · Under choice 3, production's opening rule is probed with a price (D191 point 4, D368 item 1) on its stored requests (council consensus under D439)\n5441:## D481 · 2026-11-13 · The production price change fails and stops; next a $0 census of the opening losses by what the article states (council consensus under D439)\n5453:## D482 · 2026-11-13 · No further paid test on this ruler today; production stays the default; the measured map goes to Alex (council consensus under D439)\n5902:## D509 · 2026-11-15 · Alex goes inactive: Claude operates by his rules, and every round's run is examined in depth with the council (D439 in force again)\n5921:## D510 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the six-call test of one missing fact's effect on one stored judgement is sent (council consensus)\n5935:## D511 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the six-call test is inconclusive; no change and no further send on the delivery line; a cold reflection council comes next (council consensus)\n5952:## D512 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the reflection council's consensus: a decision page for Alex comes first; no further reading or send before it (council consensus)\n6005:## D515 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the decision page is the reflection council's outcome; nothing further is sent or run on the lean path until Alex answers it (council consensus)\n6023:## D516 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: D515's wait is superseded; the next step is a $0 sizing and design of the comparison, reviewed by the council before any send (council consensus)\n6043:## D517 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the comparison is sized and not sent; the next step is a side-by-side of the two systems' output on the fresh week, then a bounded council decision (council consensus)\n6064:## D518 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the default and both systems stay (a bounded council decision); the side-by-side is corrected; the next investigation is a $0 census of unsupported judgements (council consensus, reflection round 8)\n6083:## D519 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the side-by-side