nswer choices are run; the matching and the judge are recorded as not run (council consensus)\n6860:## D554 · 2026-11-15 · The one-week diagnostic of the answer choices is read: not clean on both counts; recorded as evidence, not as a gate (under D439)\n6884:## D555 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the work stays on the new system; the next step is a $0 study of the boundary of \"no main part\"; no first-named rule, no change to the frozen step, no send (council consensus)\n6907:## D556 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: no candidate for the \"no main part\" refusals among those considered; next, at $0, one map of every stored topic that falls short of the first gate, with overlapping and unresolved causes (council consensus)\n6930:## D557 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the map of the first gate is accepted with one correction; Alex's lines stay as written and no pass is claimed; next, at $0, one prompt audit of the two classes that are the answer-choice step's own (council consensus)\n6955:## D558 · 2026-11-15 · Under D439: the audit of the two classes finds no repair ready; the first gate is recorded as unmet with Alex's lines unchanged; one question and one next step go to Alex (council consensus)\n7198:## D565 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the six contested answers traced; D520's open choice turned into one bounded diagnostic of the frozen judge's self-report (council consensus, rounds 12 to 16)\n7216:## D566 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the D520 line closed with its record for Alex; a production closing defect fixed; the new system's daily loop to close due questions as production does (council consensus, rounds 17 to 24)\n7237:## D567 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the new system closes due questions as production does; the integration slice accepted (council consensus, rounds 25 and 26)\n7256:## D568 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: a repeatability check of gate 1's reading on the fortnight (council consensus, rounds 27 to 31)\n7272:## D569 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: gate 1's verdict reproduced by its method on the fortnight; D397's display of the parts not judged is missing from the product, the next work (council consensus on the course, round 32)\n7289:## D570 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: D397's display built and unit-proved, its browser proof pending; the product page refuses the new system's three-choice events; next, the page contract for the new system's answer shapes (council consensus, rounds 33 to 37)\n7309:## D571 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the product page reads the new system's questions without inventing a direction, and shows D397's parts not judged (council consensus on the designs, rounds 38 to 40)\n7326:## D572 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the two page slices accepted after their fixes and drawer checks; next, the actual serving path on a new-system store (council consensus, rounds 41 to 43)\n7341:## D573 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the product's API serves a new-system store to the page; next, serving while a stored replay writes (council consensus, round 44)\n7357:## D574 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: a freshly opened page shows the served library's latest completed day; the first day of a live store is an open defect; next, the live-service design (council consensus, rounds 45 to 50)\n7377:## D575 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the live-service design paused as recorded input; a consolidated page for Alex now; then a $0 feasibility census for Stage B's control line, no paid send implied (council consensus, rounds 51 and 52)\n7393:## D576 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: Stage B's control line cannot be exercised by re-sending the judge; no delivery check; next, at $0, a census of the unlisted-parts class now that the page reads the list (council consensus, rounds 53 to 58)\n7412:## D577 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the unlisted-parts probe of arm A is sent and read as designed (council consensus, rounds 59 to 65)\n7431:## D578 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: arm A's probe is negative and the line stops; two bounded accounts of its refusals are run before any further design (council consensus, round 66)\n7448:## D579 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the refusal accounts read; no A2 rule yet; a bounded $0 audit of the decline rules and the outcome's extra parts first (council consensus, round 67)\n7467:## D580 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: no reviewed repair for the unlisted parts; arm A stays stopped; next, a $0 check of the Idea planner on new-system answer shapes (council consensus, rounds 68 and 69)\n7487:## D581 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the event-driver design parked as recorded input; paid work and new lines held until Alex returns or the council names a gate-moving candidate (council consensus, rounds 70 to 72)\n8017:## D604 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 145): the next production step is a $0 trace of why the fresh topics fail line 5, before any candidate\n8037:## D605 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council rounds 146 and 147): D604's line-5 route closes with no candidate; the gate stays unmet, and paid work is held pending new evidence or Alex's rulings\n8060:## D606 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 148): the items on Alex's page that D439 permits are decided reversibly; next, a $0 audit of the postponed-event class\n8091:## D607 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 149): D606's postponement reading is reversed provisionally; the postponement repair route closes; next, a $0 audit of the shared fiscal-year note\n8113:## D608 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 150): the fiscal-note lead closes as cleanup-only with no demonstrated product effect; a reflection council reads the record cold\n8129:## D609 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (reflection council, fresh Codex thread 01a1e644): the next production step is a $0 source-to-request trace of the company's own figures on the carried fortnight (D505's delivery), with time, duplicate, population and relevance controls\n8152:## D610 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (reflection council, challenge 2): the company-figure delivery route closes, narrowly; the v12 effect test is not sent; next, a $0 feasibility review of a same-news product comparison from established libraries\n8171:## D611 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439: the same-news comparison from established libraries is not feasible within D439's remainder and closes by D610's condition\n8180:## D612 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 151): paid work is held on the candidates the evidence now supports; the running system stays the default; work reopens on four named conditions\n8197:## D613 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 152): D611's exposure claim corrected; D612's hold stands; no code check or send on gate 1's six failing sends\n8213:## D614 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 153): the refusal census maps to the closed main-part class; D612 stands; next, a $0 design review of splitting against D397, D436 and D38\n8231:## D615 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council round 154): the period split is developed at $0 as a lead on D397's open defect; no gate movement claimed, no probe authorized\n8249:## D616 · 2026-11-16 · Under D439 (council rounds 155 to 158): the period split's design v4 is accepted for a $0 scratch build; the narrow D397 departure is recorded as a reversible proposal; nothing is sent\n9116:## D655 · 2026-11-17 · Council consensus (D439, D654): send the paired test of the narrow passage v5.5 on astra, shared cap $3.60\n9460:## D667 · 2026-11-17 · Under D666 and D439 (council, run-plan rounds 1–10): the release comparison's run plan and the rules it takes for this run\n10042:## D677 · 2026-11-19 · The release comparison's goal loop is closed; the old system stays; no paid work continues (council consensus, D439/D544)\n11484:## D745 · 2026-11-23 · The D744 re-read calibrates the readers but stops on a qualifier-list gap and on S's unsupported share; council 59 recommends a targeted $0 test of one clarification, for Alex to authorize\n11524:## D746 · 2026-11-23 · The D745 targeted test fails on E's unsized cut; S splits on how far an indirect comparison can support a forecast; council 61–61b: one general question to Alex, then a $0 stored-answer re-read; the paid re-send stays on hold\n11573:## D747 · 2026-11-23 · Alex rules that a forecast may rest on an explained indirect comparison\n11592:## D748 · 2026-11-23 · The D747 re-read fails on a self-contradicting floor; three of four earlier splits settle under the ruling; council 63: ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair; the paid re-send stays on hold\n11641:## D749 · 2026-11-23 · Alex authorizes the E writer repair and its $0 writer test\n11656:## D750 · 2026-11-23 · The D749 writer test is INCONCLUSIVE with no failed line; council 65 (under D439): one bullet-2 sentence on reaffirmed targets, then a second $0 writer test\n---\nname: prompt-audit\ndescription: After every measurement of an extraction configuration, and before any prompt change, map each failure class in the stored draws to the sentence of the request that produced it, check that sentence against the frozen standard and the prompt principles, and write the audit table. Alex, 2026-11-02 - \"你应该看着prompt，然后对比失败的trace，然后仔细的根据尺子做对比，并且我们prompt的principle也要带入，是尝试教他general hedge fund analyst skill，不是要hardcode或是benchmark farming；你把这个写成一个skill以后固定跑\".\n---\n\n# Prompt audit: failures → the request's sentences → the standard → the principle\n\nRun this after every measured configuration (three draws scored on the frozen ruler) and before any edit to a prompt file, a schema\ndescription or a takes line. A measurement without this audit is a score without a diagnosis (AGENTS §7.2, §6). The audit is read,\nnot scripted: the scripts below only produce the lists to read.\n\n## 0. Inputs\n\n- The arm's run folders (`docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/arms/<arm>/d1..3`) and the baseline's.\n- The frozen ruler (AGENTS §7.1): the extraction standard `docs/prd/05-extraction-standard.html` (version 3, D243, with D250's\n  boundaries), golden-v5, the questions standard, the judgement gold. Never edited; every disagreement is a gap in the system.\n- The prompt principles (AGENTS §6 and §8): the prompt carries the standard and no new rule; it teaches a general hedge-fund\n  analyst, so every sentence and example reads the same for a bank, a drug maker, a retailer or a chip maker, names no covered\n  company, product or number, and takes no example from a test article; a classification is a closed set with examples; never grow a\n  prompt to fix quality without cutting as much elsewhere; a field's definition sits in the schema beside the field; code owns\n  identity, never importance.\n\n## 1. Dump the request as the model reads it\n\nOne stored request of the configuration (any article), printed whole: the system text (the role), every user block before the item\n(category block, subjects, research reference, open questions with their takes lines, research groups), the closing sentence, the\nend-of-request check, and every schema field description (evidence and candidates). Read it top to bottom once. List every\ninstruction that decides keep, reject, link, open, or a field value, with its location (role paragraph, check row, schema field,\ntakes line, category block). This list is the thing the failures are mapped onto.\n\n```sh\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport sqlite3, json\na = sqlite3.connect('file:<run folder>/archive.sqlite?mode=ro', uri=True)\nreq = json.loads(a.execute(\"select request_json from model_calls where purpose='extract' and request_json like '%<title fragment>%' order by call_id desc limit 1\").fetchone()[0])\nprint(req['messages'][0]['content']); print(req['messages'][1]['content'].split('[Item]')[0]); print(req['messages'][1]['content'].rsplit('\\n\\n', 2)[-2:])\nprint(json.dumps({k: v.get('description') for k, v in req['response_format']['json_schema']['schema']['properties']['evidence']['items']['properties'].items() if v.get('description')}, ensure_ascii=False, indent=1))\nPY\n```\n\n## 2. Produce the failure lists (all at no model cost, on the stored draws)\n\n| List | Script | What it gives |\n|---|---|---|\n| Matter states across draws | `harness/matter_states.py arm=d1,d2,d3 base=d1,d2,d3` | every gold core/supporting matter: extracted or reaching in 3/2/1/0 draws; the systematic misses (0 of 3) and the coin flips (1 of 3) |\n| Written noise by the standard's row | the `rows_all` count in `design-v72.md` §10 (the gold's `not_kept[].row`) | which row of the standard the written noise falls under, with examples |\n| No-home drops | `harness/dropped_census.py d1 d2 d3` | gold matters written but dropped, with the questions open at the time |\n| Where links go | `harness/links_by_question.py d1 d2 d3 --sample 20` | the pile per question, the revenue-sink share, statements under several questions, noise under revenue |\n| Quote refusals | the `dropped` reasons of the handovers (`quote not in item`), each diffed against its closest source window | paraphrase against a word or two off |\n| Question recall | `harness/question_recall.py d1 d2 d3` | must_open / may_open covered by seeds and by article-opened questions |\n| Fields | 15 random stored statements with speaker, original_who, original_day, tier | read against the quote and the item's day and publisher |\n\nFor every list, read the items, not the counts: the raw answer beside the article for every systematic miss (a miss the scorer reports\nmay be the matter written in other words: check before counting it), a sample of twenty for every pile.\n\n## 3. Map each failure class to the request\n\nFor each class with more than a handful of cases, fill one row:\n\n| Failure class (count, share) | The sentence(s) of the request that produced it, quoted | The standard's line on the same case (section, decision) | Verdict | The model's own account (when the sentence is not obvious) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n\nVerdicts, one of: **contradiction** (two sentences of the request pull opposite ways, or a request sentence removes what the standard\nkeeps, D240), **missing** (no sentence decides the case; the model guesses, a coin flip per send), **abstract** (a clause without an\nexample, read differently each send), **misread** (the sentence is right, the model does not apply it; needs the model's own account\nbefore any change), **not the prompt** (code, scorer or sampler).\n\nThe model's own account: continue the stored conversation with one question about one case (`harness/probe_v72_link.py`,\n`probe_v72_missing.py`), a cent a case, for every \"misread\" and for any class whose sentence is not obvious from reading.\n\n## 4. Check every proposed fix against the principles before writing it\n\n- It is written from the standard's line, not from the failing article: the example comes from another domain, names no covered\n  company, product or number, and reads the same for every industry. A fix that only recovers the bench's misses is benchmark\n  farming and is not written.\n- It removes a contradiction, supplies a missing definition at its owner (schema field, takes line, check row, category block), or\n  replaces an abstract clause with a closed set and examples. It never adds a rule the standard does not hold.\n- It cuts at least as much as it adds, or the growth has a written reason; report characters before and after.\n- One class per change; the change is proved on the stored requests of that class, three sends as stored against three changed,\n  with the noise guards of the same articles; the whole bench accepts it (three draws) only when Alex asks for a run.\n\n## 5. Output\n\nWrite the table and the verdicts into the arm's design document (a numbered section), one row per class, in the order of the loss;\nthe report to Alex states each class in a reader's words (what the system does wrong, which sentence makes it do that, what the\nstandard says), never in the loop's own words (AGENTS, \"Authority and scope\": explain as to a sixteen-year-old).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd; git status --short; ls -a .claude/skills/prompt-audit; rg --files | rg 'blind[56]\\\\.py|BLIND5-RESULT|codex-r65|SMALL-DESIGN|judging-v13s|10-filing-phase|CURRENT_STATE|AGENTS.md|DECISIONS.md'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"pwd; git status --short; ls -a .claude/skills/prompt-audit; rg --files | rg 'blind[56]\\\\.py|BLIND5-RESULT|codex-r65|SMALL-DESIGN|judging-v13s|10-filing-phase|CURRENT_STATE|AGENTS.md|DECISIONS.md'\"","aggregated_output":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-JoqzoHhj' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-23 01:15:43.049 xcodebuild[40070:74637013]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-23 01:15:43.217 xcodebuild[40070:74637011] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-JUWKYQoP' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-11-23 01:15:43.577 xcodebuild[40075:74637057]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-11-23 01:15:43.689 xcodebuild[40075:74637056] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n M docs/CURRENT_STATE.md\n M docs/DECISIONS-log.md\n M docs/DECISIONS.md\n?? docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/\n.\n..\nSKILL.md\nAGENTS.md\ndocs/DECISIONS.md\ndocs/archive/2026-10-22-v15/DECISIONS.md\ndocs/prd/10-filing-phase.md\ndocs/archive/2026-10-22-v15/CURRENT_STATE.md\ndocs/CURRENT_STATE.md\ndocs/archive/2026-10-16-v1/DECISIONS.md\ndocs/archive/2026-10-16-v1/CURRENT_STATE.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind6.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s-d745.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r65.md\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r65.stream\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s-d749.txt\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py\ndocs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND5-RESULT.md\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
