{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/DECISIONS-log.md | sed -n '11484,\"'$p'\"'\"","aggregated_output":" 11484\t## D745 · 2026-11-23 · The D744 re-read calibrates the readers but stops on a qualifier-list gap and on S's unsupported share; council 59 recommends a targeted $0 test of one clarification, for Alex to authorize\n 11485\t\n 11486\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md` §5; `REREAD2-TALLY.json`):\n 11487\t  - **The readers are calibrated.**\n 11488\t    - All five controls passed: midpoint, 108.5 misread, overlap, disjoint, unsupported assumption.\n 11489\t    - No defect was marked by both readers on the 12 replies.\n 11490\t  - **STOP on two lines, as written:**\n 11491\t    1. T10 (S, Claude writer) F11: \"an estimated $750 billion\" recorded with qualifier \"none\". Both adjudicators upheld it. \"estimated\" is\n 11492\t       not in the closed qualifier list, so the format forced \"none\". This is 1 affected figure of 251 source figures in the three writer\n 11493\t       runs.\n 11494\t    2. S has zero usable replies. Both writers state a data-center share of total capex (90%; 95–100%) that the passages do not size, and\n 11495\t       the share decides the band.\n 11496\t  - **E's Codex reply** is now \"not supported\": its 15% cut from the guided floor decides the band. This is the same weakness.\n 11497\t- **Council round 59** (`codex-r59.md`) chose a targeted $0 test, (c), over Claude's lean to go to Alex for the paid re-send, (b):\n 11498\t  - Going straight to the paid re-send would measure the known weakness in gpt-6-luna without the request saying what a supported size\n 11499\t    is.\n 11500\t  - Skipping a clean result needs Alex to change the registered sequence anyway.\n 11501\t  - Claude agrees: the weakness is unsupported precision in a number that decides the rung, which is the goal's own failure (D725).\n 11502\t- **Proposed test (for Alex to authorize):**\n 11503\t  1. Add \"estimated\" to the qualifier list, and show readers the allowed values. Prove it on the saved replies, with a case and a\n 11504\t     mutant.\n 11505\t  2. Add one clarification to the existing instruction: when a deduction or cut decides the band, show the evidence for its size or a\n 11506\t     bound the passages support that justifies the band; if neither, answer unresolved.\n 11507\t  3. Test on S and on one stored case where the passages do support a narrower figure.\n 11508\t  4. Before the test, Alex rules whether a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n 11509\t  - Falsifier: a fresh S answer still picks a band on an unsupported share, or the supported case is withheld.\n 11510\t- **Alex's answers** (2026-11-23):\n 11511\t  - to \"怎么走？\": \"批准针对性小测 (推荐)\". The other options were \"不小测，直接议花钱重发\" and \"先停在这里\".\n 11512\t  - to whether a justified \"无法判断\" counts: \"算合格 (推荐)\". The other option was \"不算\".\n 11513\t- **Decided (Alex):**\n 11514\t  1. Run the targeted $0 test.\n 11515\t  2. An unresolved answer whose reason shows the passages cannot settle the rung counts as a usable answer.\n 11516\t- **Council round 60** (`codex-r60.md`) set the wording and the registration (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D745]):\n 11517\t  - Rung-deciding shares, deductions and discounts must show their passage support or a justifying bound, else unresolved.\n 11518\t  - The default discount is made subject to that rule.\n 11519\t  - The three controls are the saved E 15% cut, a vague P-v8 unresolved answer and a justified S unresolved answer (expected no, no,\n 11520\t    yes).\n 11521\t  - Pass: every S and E reply settled yes on a forecast or its reason; both P-v8 replies settled yes on a forecast. A support split\n 11522\t    is inconclusive.\n 11523\t\n 11524\t## D746 · 2026-11-23 · The D745 targeted test fails on E's unsized cut; S splits on how far an indirect comparison can support a forecast; council 61–61b: one general question to Alex, then a $0 stored-answer re-read; the paid re-send stays on hold\n 11525\t\n 11526\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md`; run `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/`,\n 11527\t  `TALLY.json`):\n 11528\t  - **FAIL on a registered line.** E's Codex reply (rung 3, $36B) realises 90% of the $40B reference and itself says \"the passages\n 11529\t    give no order sizes or shipment pace\". Both first readers marked it not supported.\n 11530\t  - **Four splits, all along model family** (8 of 8 adjudicator votes went with their own family): S Claude (98% share), S Codex ($25B\n 11531\t    deduction), E Claude (1.8x with a 90% Vera share) and the justified-unresolved S control.\n 11532\t  - **The rest:**\n 11533\t    - P-v8: 2 of 2 supported;\n 11534\t    - the unsupported-cut and vague-unresolved controls read as expected;\n 11535\t    - no refusal, no defect;\n 11536\t    - 0 of 6 replies withheld.\n 11537\t  - **One construction change, disclosed.** The justified-unresolved control was rebuilt on the third run's S Codex reply, because the\n 11538\t    S Claude reply is refused by the current code (S1). Its reason text is unchanged.\n 11539\t- **Council rounds 61 and 61b** (`claude-r61.md`, `codex-r61.md`, `codex-r61b.md`) reached consensus:\n 11540\t  - **The FAIL stands.** Resolving every split would still leave E's Codex reply failed.\n 11541\t  - **Two problems.**\n 11542\t    1. **The reading standard is not settled.** The open point is how far a related figure can support a forecast when the passages do\n 11543\t       not measure the asked quantity on the deciding side.\n 11544\t       - S has split this way in three readings: \"more than $730B on AI infrastructure\" for the same four companies, as a floor for\n 11545\t         their data-center spending.\n 11546\t       - E Claude's bracket fails on its own assumptions ($20B × 1.5 × 90% = $27B, rung 4). That point is arithmetic.\n 11547\t       - D741 ruling 3 still requires a stated deduction or a supported bound. The threshold for \"supported\" when the support is an\n 11548\t         indirect comparison is Alex's to set.\n 11549\t    2. **Writers size a risk without evidence.** 3 of 4 E replies across two runs carry a disputed cut or share, and D745's sentence\n 11550\t       did not stop it.\n 11551\t  - **Corrections.**\n 11552\t    - Claude withdrew two reasons for the lean. D725 does not promise that code catches every invented figure. AGENTS §8's \"no data to\n 11553\t      verify\" concerns outcomes after the fact.\n 11554\t    - The result page was corrected in three places: U05 had two first readers; unresolved singletons are published and inspected; the\n 11555\t      paid S asks about CY2027.\n 11556\t    - Whether a paid STOP is predictable: it is a conditional risk, not a measured rate (Codex; Claude agrees).\n 11557\t  - **The recommendation.** Ask Alex one general question (below), with a lean to allow the forecast when the answer explains why the\n 11558\t    comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked, and why, under its own assumptions, that side of the line\n 11559\t    is more likely.\n 11560\t  - **The one test after his ruling.** A $0 blinded re-read of nine stored answers under his words, added to the shared definitions:\n 11561\t    - the answers: U01–U06, U08, the third run's T10 (for its spending argument only), and T15 (the accepted E bracket);\n 11562\t    - fresh readers, one per family;\n 11563\t    - what his choice implies for each answer is recorded before reading.\n 11564\t    - It moves on to a writer repair only if both families apply his words alike. A continuing split leaves the publication question\n 11565\t      open in practice. A clean re-read does not turn D745 into a pass.\n 11566\t  - **The paid re-send stays on hold** until an E writer repair passes a clean $0 test. The proposed repair: the writer chooses between\n 11567\t    a forecast and \"can't tell\" before it assigns a discount, naming what makes one side more likely under its own assumptions. It is a\n 11568\t    new arm and goes to council before any send. Publishing management's figure whenever it sits on a cutoff would change the product,\n 11569\t    and needs Alex's own decision.\n 11570\t- **The question to Alex** (pending): \"资料没直接给出所问的数。用一个相关数字作比较，能解释为什么结果更可能在线的这一边，但另一边仍有可能。这时可以发布预测，还是要等到能从资料算出结果落在线的哪一边？\"\n 11571\t- **Not done.** Nothing was paid. Nothing was tuned on the 36 stored answers. The request was not changed after the registration.\n 11572\t\n 11573\t## D747 · 2026-11-23 · Alex rules that a forecast may rest on an explained indirect comparison\n 11574\t\n 11575\t- **The question** (after D746): \"资料没直接给出题目问的那个数，只能拿一个相关的数字来比。比如问四大云厂商今年的数据中心开支能不能过 7000 亿，资料只说“这四家 AI 基础设施开支超过 7300 亿”。这种比较能说明结果更可能落在线的某一边，但另一边也还有可能。这时系统可以发布预测吗，还是要等资料能直接算出落在哪边？\"\n 11576\t  - Options:\n 11577\t    - \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\": the answer must explain why the comparison applies to the companies, the year and the quantity\n 11578\t      asked, and why, under its own assumptions, that side is more likely; an answer that cannot explain it is not supported;\n 11579\t    - \"先说“还判断不了”\";\n 11580\t    - \"先停在这里\".\n 11581\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"可以发布，要讲清楚 (推荐)\".\n 11582\t- **Decided (Alex).** When the passages do not give the asked quantity, a forecast may rest on a related figure. It is supported\n 11583\t  only when the answer explains two things: why the comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked; and why,\n 11584\t  under the answer's own stated assumptions, the chosen side of the line is more likely. An answer that cannot explain this is not\n 11585\t  supported.\n 11586\t  - D741 ruling 3 still holds: a total used for a narrower quantity states the deduction as its own figure, or gives a supported\n 11587\t    bound.\n 11588\t  - D745's ruling still holds: a justified unresolved answer counts as usable.\n 11589\t- **Next (D746).** The ruling's words go into the shared reader definitions (`blind_rules.py`). Then one $0 blinded re-read of nine\n 11590\t  stored answers, registered with its expected readings and reviewed by the council before any packet is read.\n 11591\t\n 11592\t## D748 · 2026-11-23 · The D747 re-read fails on a self-contradicting floor; three of four earlier splits settle under the ruling; council 63: ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair; the paid re-send stays on hold\n 11593\t\n 11594\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md` §6; `REREAD-TALLY.json`, `reread-reasons.json`):\n 11595\t  - **FAIL on the stop line.** On U02 (S, Claude writer), both adjudicators upheld \"part above or added into its whole\". The answer\n 11596\t    calls \"more than $730B\" of AI infrastructure \"the supported floor\" for data-center spending, while its own total spending is $720B\n 11597\t    and its data-center outcome $705.6B.\n 11598\t    - The code did not catch it. The figure is linked only to the 98% share, and the floor is claimed in prose. D738 leaves that\n 11599\t      reading to readers.\n 11600\t    - In the 18 stored blind replies this explicit defect occurs once (Codex, council 63).\n 11601\t  - **Six of nine settle with compatible reasons**, and each fixed reading that settled matched its registration:\n 11602\t    - U01, U03 and U05: no;\n 11603\t    - U06: no;\n 11604\t    - U04 (justified unresolved): yes;\n 11605\t    - U08 ($25B deduction explained by the same companies' AI-infrastructure figure and Meta's share): yes.\n 11606\t  - **Three of the four answers that split in the targeted test now settle** (U04, U06, U08).\n 11607\t  - **Three splits remain:** T10, T15 and U02's support vote.\n 11608\t    - All six adjudicator votes followed their own family's first vote. Which family was stricter changed with the question: Codex on\n 11609\t      S, Claude on E.\n 11610\t    - T15 had been accepted in all three earlier readings.\n 11611\t- **A process error** (Claude and council 62). The registration required five boundary answers to settle, or to settle as expected,\n 11612\t  without estimating how often readers split on boundary answers (AGENTS §7.1, \"a conjunction over many items fails by chance\"). The\n 11613\t  stop on U02 does not depend on it.\n 11614\t- **Council round 63** (`claude-r63.md`, `codex-r63.md`) reached consensus:\n 11615\t  - **The FAIL stands. No further reader round.** Another vote on the same nine answers leaves the writers untouched.\n 11616\t  - **Claude conceded three points.**\n 11617\t    - The remaining splits are not shown to be random variation. T10 and T15 turn on judgement over \"explains why\" and \"more likely\".\n 11618\t      On U02, one side accepted the band and the other required the writer's stated route. D747 already rejects U02's route. No\n 11619\t      missing general clause was found.\n 11620\t    - A writer test with registered lines only on stable readings would let a repeat of U05's invented cut through. Each fresh E and\n 11621\t      S answer must earn agreement for its forecast or for its specific reason for \"can't tell\".\n 11622\t    - Changing the calculation format for prose-claimed bounds is deferred. One case does not establish it, and U08 shows that an\n 11623\t      indirect comparison must stay able to inform a forecast without becoming a binding minimum. U02 becomes a control instead.\n 11624\t  - **The recommendation.** Ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair despite the three disclosed splits. D746 made the repair\n 11625\t    conditional on reader agreement, so going ahead needs his decision.\n 11626\t    - The repair: the writer decides whether the evidence favours one side of the line before it chooses a discount. If it can\n 11627\t      explain only why sales might fall short, it says what remains unknown.\n 11628\t    - The changed request goes to the council before any send.\n 11629\t  - **The one test after approval.** A $0 blind test:\n 11630\t    - fresh Codex and Claude writers on E, S and P-v8;\n 11631\t    - the saved U05 and U02 mixed in as controls for an invented cut and an impossible floor.\n 11632\t    - To pass:\n 11633\t      - each fresh E and S answer earns agreement for its forecast or its specific \"can't tell\" reason;\n 11634\t      - both P-v8 answers are supported forecasts;\n 11635\t      - the code accepts the fresh replies;\n 11636\t      - no confirmed defect survives.\n 11637\t    - A settled unsupported answer or a contradictory floor fails. A persistent split is inconclusive. Only a clean result supports\n 11638\t      asking Alex for the paid re-send.\n 11639\t- **Not done.** Nothing was paid. No request text was changed.\n 11640\t\n 11641\t## D749 · 2026-11-23 · Alex authorizes the E writer repair and its $0 writer test\n 11642\t\n 11643\t- **The question** (after D748): \"下一步怎么走？\"\n 11644\t  - Options:\n 11645\t    - \"批准修写手再小测 (推荐)\": the writer first decides whether the evidence favours one side of the line, then whether to discount;\n 11646\t      if it can only say sales might fall short, it answers \"can't tell\" and says what is missing. The changed request goes to the\n 11647\t      council, then one $0 writer test on E, S and P with the two failed answers as controls. A clean pass comes back to Alex for the\n 11648\t      paid re-send.\n 11649\t    - \"不修，直接议花钱重发\".\n 11650\t    - \"先停在这里\".\n 11651\t- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-23): \"批准修写手再小测 (推荐)\".\n 11652\t- **Decided (Alex).** Repair the writer request as council 63 described. Review it in council before any send. Then run one $0\n 11653\t  blind writer test on E, S and P-v8, with the saved U05 (invented cut) and U02 (impossible floor) as reader controls, under D748's\n 11654\t  pass lines. The paid re-send stays on hold until that test passes clean.\n 11655\t\n 11656\t## D750 · 2026-11-23 · The D749 writer test is INCONCLUSIVE with no failed line; council 65 (under D439): one bullet-2 sentence on reaffirmed targets, then a second $0 writer test\n 11657\t\n 11658\t- **Alex's direction** (2026-11-23, before sleeping): \"你接下来开始自行收敛，方向吧，我要准备睡了，所以这边的决策交给你，还有 Council， 记得不要 Scope Drift， 我们的目标是把剩下有问题的地方收敛起来，然后准备要往 Production 方向去走了，所以你自己每次复习的时候看 Log， 看我们试过了哪些东西，不要犯一模一样的错误，然后赶紧的往收敛方向去做测量和把它定下来。\"\n 11659\t  - D439 governs: the council decides reversibly, no paid send (its ceiling is spent), nothing committed.\n 11660\t- **The result** (`docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND5-RESULT.md`; run `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/`):\n 11661\t  - **The repair worked where it was aimed.**\n 11662\t    - E's Codex writer, which invented a cut in both earlier runs, now answers a justified unresolved, accepted by both families.\n 11663\t    - Both P-v8 replies are supported forecasts.\n 11664\t    - Both controls were caught: the invented cut settled no, and the impossible floor was upheld by both adjudicators.\n 11665\t    - No fresh defect, no refusal. S's Codex forecast is supported.\n 11666\t  - **Two splits:**\n 11667\t    - X05, E Claude, takes a not-yet-shipping target in full, asserting \"already selling at volume\". No passage shows shipments,\n 11668\t      revenue to date or orders.\n 11669\t    - X08, S Claude: one reader cites \"more than $730B\" as a floor above its own $710.4B outcome, the other reads it as a guide.\n 11670\t- **Claude's error, corrected.** I first recorded X08's reasons as compatible although my own note named the tension. Council 65\n 11671\t  caught it. X08 was then adjudicated as registered and stayed split.\n 11672\t- **Council round 65** (`claude-r65.md`, `codex-r65.md`) reached consensus:\n 11673\t  - X05's premise is a question of fact under the existing rule, not a gap in Alex's words.\n 11674\t  - Claude's closed list of \"volume in hand\" was rejected: it was wider and narrower than the standard at once.\n 11675\t  - The smaller sentence is at bullet 2: \"it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence\n 11676\t    puts the required volume in hand for the period\".\n 11677\t  - One $0 writer test on all three cases (Alex's three-case condition), with the same controls and lines. On S, a reading that cites a\n 11678\t    floor above the answer's own outcome is not compatible with one that reads a guide.\n 11679\t  - The paid re-send stays on hold.\n 11680\t- **Done.** The sentence was changed (4,794 → 4,867 characters). Cases 111 of 111, rehearsal 19 of 19, pinned plan unchanged. The test\n 11681\t  is registered (`SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D750]) and built by `blind6.py`. Council round 66 reviews it before any send.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba SMALL-DESIGN.md | tail -185; rg -n 'D750|D749|D747|D745' ../../CURRENT_STATE.md ../../DECISIONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && for f in judging-v13s.txt blind6.py blind5.py BLIND5-RESULT.md codex-r65.md; do echo \"$f\"; nl -ba \"$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && for f in judging-v13s.txt blind6.py blind5.py BLIND5-RESULT.md codex-r65.md; do echo \"$f\"; nl -ba \"$f\"; done'","aggregated_output":"judging-v13s.txt\n     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\n     4\t- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate whose pace you forecast, informed by guidance, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted subject to the evidence requirement below; it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence puts the required volume in hand for the period. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input, not an answer: weigh time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say) under the evidence requirement below; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- \"Themes in force\" lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on a member and report it in that member's theme_pushes with the direction it pushes that member (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \"updated since this thesis was last judged\" may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- Your conclusions must be consistent with each other and with the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open.\n     9\t- Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge rather than read or compute is an estimate, stated as yours. Before sizing a share, deduction, discount or pace that decides the band, explain which band the evidence favours. Show support for the size or a justifying bound. If the passages lack the quantity asked, explain why a related figure fits the companies, period and quantity, and why your assumptions favour that band. If you can say only that the outcome might fall short or overshoot, not which band is more likely, answer unresolved and name what is unknown. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\nblind6.py\n     1\t\"\"\"The D750 $0 writer test (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5 [D750]): blind5's design, unchanged, on the request with council 65's bullet-2 sentence\n     2\t(\"it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence puts the required volume in hand for the\n     3\tperiod\"). Cases S, E and P-v8; a fresh Claude and Codex writer each; the same two reader controls; the same tally.\n     4\t\n     5\t  python3 blind6.py build|check|packets|tally <out>\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\timport sys\n     8\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     9\t\n    10\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    11\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    12\timport blind5  # noqa: E402\n    13\t\n    14\tblind5.REQUEST_SHA256 = '54f5847d715caec159e6509b7966c13df4d4af0756953d206fefa1347879f397'   # judging-v13s.txt as registered (D750)\n    15\tblind5.READER_BRIEF = blind5.READER_BRIEF.replace('writer test, D749', 'writer test, D750')\n    16\tif 'D750' not in blind5.READER_BRIEF:\n    17\t    raise SystemExit('the D750 reader brief is not built')\n    18\t\n    19\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    20\t    cmd = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) == 3 else ''\n    21\t    target = Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve() if len(sys.argv) == 3 else None\n    22\t    {'build': blind5.build, 'check': blind5.check, 'packets': blind5.packets, 'tally': blind5.tally}.get(\n    23\t        cmd, lambda _: (_ for _ in ()).throw(SystemExit(__doc__)))(target)\nblind5.py\n     1\t\"\"\"The D749 $0 writer test (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5 [D749]): cases S, E and P-v8 built from the repaired request (judging-v13s.txt, the\n     2\t\"decide the side before you size it\" sentence), a fresh Claude and Codex writer each, readers under the D747 definitions, and two\n     3\treader controls carried from the targeted test with the request they were written for: U05 (E Codex, an invented 10% cut; expected\n     4\tnot supported) and U02 (S Claude, a floor above its own total; expected the part-above-whole defect upheld).\n     5\t\n     6\t  python3 blind5.py build <out>      # the three requests and writer prompts (refuses an existing folder)\n     7\t  python3 blind5.py check <out>      # every first answer through the schema, from_answer, check and publish_decision\n     8\t  python3 blind5.py packets <out>    # 6 replies + 2 controls, shuffled X01–X08; key beside\n     9\t  python3 blind5.py tally <out>      # the registered lines, after readings, recorded reasons and any adjudication\n    10\t\"\"\"\n    11\timport hashlib\n    12\timport json\n    13\timport random\n    14\timport sys\n    15\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    16\t\n    17\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    18\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    19\timport blind4 as b4  # noqa: E402\n    20\tfrom blind_rules import format_material  # noqa: E402\n    21\t\n    22\tCASES = b4.CASES                                                     # ('S', 'E', 'P-v8')\n    23\tBLIND4 = HERE.parents[2] / 'poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23'\n    24\tCONTROLS = {'K-invented-cut': ('E', 'codex'), 'K-impossible-floor': ('S', 'claude')}     # blind4 U05 and U02, unchanged\n    25\tFLOOR_DEFECT = ('part above or added into its whole', ('F11', 'F12', 'F15'))\n    26\tREADER_BRIEF = b4.REREAD_BRIEF.replace('re-read under the comparison ruling, D747', 'writer test, D749')\n    27\tREQUEST_SHA256 = 'ac707fa96890cee1f69dcf84e6c5242ec014b00b502214ece84b1318252a9859'   # judging-v13s.txt as registered (council 64)\n    28\tif 'D749' not in READER_BRIEF:\n    29\t    raise SystemExit('the D749 reader brief is not built')\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\tdef build(out):\n    33\t    request = (HERE / 'judging-v13s.txt').read_bytes()\n    34\t    if hashlib.sha256(request).hexdigest() != REQUEST_SHA256:\n    35\t        raise SystemExit('judging-v13s.txt is not the registered D749 request')\n    36\t    b4.build(out)\n    37\t    for name in CASES:\n    38\t        if (out / name / 'system.txt').read_bytes() != request:\n    39\t            raise SystemExit(f'{name}: the built system text is not the registered D749 request')\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef check(out):\n    43\t    b4.check(out)\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\tdef packets(out):\n    47\t    rows = json.loads((out / 'CHECKED.json').read_text())\n    48\t    unreadable = [f'{r[\"case\"]}/{r[\"writer\"]} ({r[\"stage\"]})' for r in rows if r['stage'] != 'checked']\n    49\t    if unreadable:      # a reply refused before the checks has no answer to read; the run has already failed (registered)\n    50\t        print('FAIL: first replies refused before the code checks:', ', '.join(unreadable), '- readers are not needed for the verdict')\n    51\t    items = [{'label': f'fresh {r[\"case\"]}/{r[\"writer\"]}', 'case': r['case'], 'writer': r['writer'],\n    52\t              'answer': str(out / r['case'] / 'answers' / f'{r[\"writer\"]}.json'), 'case_dir': str(out / r['case'])}\n    53\t             for r in rows if r['stage'] == 'checked']\n    54\t    for name, (case, writer) in CONTROLS.items():\n    55\t        items.append({'label': name, 'case': case, 'writer': name, 'answer': str(BLIND4 / case / 'answers' / f'{writer}.json'),\n    56\t                      'case_dir': str(BLIND4 / case)})\n    57\t    order = list(range(len(items)))\n    58\t    random.Random(hashlib.sha256(b'D749 ' + (out / 'CHECKED.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()).shuffle(order)\n    59\t    folder = out / 'reader-packets'\n    60\t    folder.mkdir(exist_ok=False)\n    61\t    key = {}\n    62\t    for n, i in enumerate(order, 1):\n    63\t        item = items[i]\n    64\t        case_dir = Path(item['case_dir'])\n    65\t        pid = f'X{n:02d}'\n    66\t        key[pid] = item\n    67\t        (folder / f'{pid}.md').write_text('\\n'.join([READER_BRIEF, format_material(case_dir), '', '# The request as the writer saw it', '',\n    68\t                                                     (case_dir / 'user.txt').read_text(), '', '# The answer', '',\n    69\t                                                     b4._display(item['answer']), '']))\n    70\t        (folder / f'{pid}.codex-prompt.txt').write_text(\n    71\t            f'Read the file {folder / f\"{pid}.md\"} and nothing else (no other file, no web). Follow the brief at its top: read the request '\n    72\t            'and the answer it contains, and return only the JSON the brief asks for, with no text before or after it.\\n')\n    73\t    (out / 'reader-key.json').write_text(json.dumps(key, indent=1))\n    74\t    print(f'{len(order)} packets in {folder}; key in reader-key.json (keep from readers)')\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef _keys(reading, floor):\n    78\t    \"\"\"A reading's defect keys; on the floor control, every part-above-whole mark naming F12 is one key (council 64).\"\"\"\n    79\t    keys = set()\n    80\t    for d in reading.get('defects', []):\n    81\t        k = b4._defect_key(d)\n    82\t        keys.add((FLOOR_DEFECT[0], ('F12',)) if floor and k[0] == FLOOR_DEFECT[0] and 'F12' in k[1] else k)\n    83\t    return keys\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\tdef _decisions(reading, floor):\n    87\t    found = {}\n    88\t    for d in reading.get('defects', []):\n    89\t        k = b4._defect_key(d)\n    90\t        k = (FLOOR_DEFECT[0], ('F12',)) if floor and k[0] == FLOOR_DEFECT[0] and 'F12' in k[1] else k\n    91\t        if found.get(k) != 'uphold':          # a key both listed as upheld and as rejected counts as upheld only if upheld once\n    92\t            found[k] = d.get('decision')\n    93\t    return found\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\tdef _vote(value, where):\n    97\t    if value not in ('yes', 'no'):\n    98\t        raise SystemExit(f'{where}: no valid vote ({value!r})')\n    99\t    return value\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef tally(out):\n   103\t    \"\"\"[D749] Scored as registered (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5 [D749], with council 64's changes).\n   104\t    Fail: a fresh reply refused or held by the code; a fresh P-v8 reply that is not a forecast; a settled no on a fresh reply; a settled\n   105\t    defect on a fresh reply; K-invented-cut not settled no; K-impossible-floor's floor defect rejected by both adjudicators or marked by\n   106\t    neither reader. Inconclusive: a support split, a defect split on a fresh reply, or a floor split left after adjudication. A settled\n   107\t    vote is final only after Claude records its two reasons as compatible (`reasons.json`).\"\"\"\n   108\t    checked = {(r['case'], r['writer']): r for r in json.loads((out / 'CHECKED.json').read_text())}\n   109\t    refused = [f'{k[0]}/{k[1]} ({v[\"stage\"]}, {v.get(\"decision\", \"-\")})' for k, v in checked.items()\n   110\t               if v['stage'] != 'checked' or v.get('decision') != 'publish']\n   111\t    if refused:                                 # decided before any reading is needed (council 64)\n   112\t        (out / 'TALLY.json').write_text(json.dumps({'verdict': 'fail', 'refused_or_held': refused}, indent=1))\n   113\t        print('fresh replies refused or held:', refused)\n   114\t        print('VERDICT: fail')\n   115\t        return\n   116\t    key = json.loads((out / 'reader-key.json').read_text())\n   117\t    expected_labels = {f'fresh {c}/{w}' for c in CASES for w in ('claude', 'codex')} | set(CONTROLS)\n   118\t    if {i['label'] for i in key.values()} != expected_labels or len(key) != len(expected_labels):\n   119\t        raise SystemExit(f'the key does not hold exactly the registered answers: {sorted(i[\"label\"] for i in key.values())}')\n   120\t    reasons_path = out / 'reasons.json'\n   121\t    reasons = json.loads(reasons_path.read_text()) if reasons_path.exists() else {}\n   122\t    lines, need, fails, splits, settled_defects, split_defects = [], [], [], [], [], []\n   123\t    floor_state = None\n   124\t    for pid, item in sorted(key.items()):\n   125\t        floor = item['label'] == 'K-impossible-floor'\n   126\t        fresh = item['label'].startswith('fresh ')\n   127\t        answer = json.loads(b4._display(item['answer']))\n   128\t        if fresh and item['case'] == 'P-v8':\n   129\t            for a in answer['answers']:\n   130\t                if a['shape'] != 'forecast':\n   131\t                    fails.append(f'{pid} {item[\"label\"]}: {a[\"view_id\"]} is {a[\"shape\"]}, not a forecast')\n   132\t        first = [b4._reading(out / 'reader-packets' / f'{pid}.{w}.json') for w in ('codex', 'claude')]\n   133\t        adjudicated = [out / 'adjudication' / f'{pid}.{w}.json' for w in ('codex', 'claude')]\n   134\t        adj = [b4._reading(p) for p in adjudicated] if all(p.exists() for p in adjudicated) else None\n   135\t        record = reasons.get(pid, {})\n   136\t        marks = [_keys(r, floor) for r in first]\n   137\t        disputed = (marks[0] | marks[1]) - (marks[0] & marks[1])\n   138\t        defect_state = {d: 'settled' for d in marks[0] & marks[1]}\n   139\t        if disputed and adj is None:\n   140\t            need.append(f'{pid} (a defect marked by one reader)')\n   141\t        elif disputed:\n   142\t            decisions = [_decisions(x, floor) for x in adj]\n   143\t            for d in disputed:\n   144\t                pair = [decisions[0].get(d), decisions[1].get(d)]\n   145\t                defect_state[d] = 'settled' if pair == ['uphold', 'uphold'] else 'rejected' if pair == ['reject', 'reject'] else 'split'\n   146\t        for d, state in defect_state.items():\n   147\t            row = [pid, item['label'], d[0], list(d[1]), state]\n   148\t            (settled_defects if state == 'settled' else split_defects if state == 'split' else []).append(row)\n   149\t            if fresh and state == 'settled':\n   150\t                fails.append(f'{pid} {item[\"label\"]}: settled defect {d[0]} {list(d[1])}')\n   151\t            if fresh and state == 'split':\n   152\t                splits.append(f'{pid} {item[\"label\"]}: defect split {d[0]} {list(d[1])}')\n   153\t        if floor:\n   154\t            floor_state = defect_state.get((FLOOR_DEFECT[0], ('F12',)), 'missed')\n   155\t        for a in answer['answers']:\n   156\t            view = a['view_id']\n   157\t            votes = [_vote(r['members'].get(view, {}).get('supported'), f'{pid} first reading') for r in first]\n   158\t            if votes[0] == votes[1] and record.get('first') == 'compatible':\n   159\t                value = votes[0]\n   160\t            elif votes[0] == votes[1] and 'first' not in record:\n   161\t                need.append(f'{pid} (reasons not yet recorded)')\n   162\t                continue\n   163\t            elif adj is None:\n   164\t                need.append(f'{pid} (support)')\n   165\t                continue\n   166\t            else:\n   167\t                second = [_vote(x['members'].get(view, {}).get('supported'), f'{pid} adjudication') for x in adj]\n   168\t                votes += second\n   169\t                if second[0] != second[1]:\n   170\t                    value = 'split'\n   171\t                elif 'adjudicated' not in record:\n   172\t                    need.append(f'{pid} (adjudicated reasons not yet recorded)')\n   173\t                    continue\n   174\t                else:\n   175\t                    value = second[0] if record['adjudicated'] == 'compatible' else 'split'\n   176\t            if item['label'] == 'K-invented-cut':\n   177\t                rule, ok = 'control expects not supported', value == 'no'\n   178\t            elif floor:\n   179\t                rule, ok = 'support not scored; the floor defect is', True\n   180\t            elif item['case'] == 'P-v8':\n   181\t                rule, ok = 'a supported forecast', a['shape'] == 'forecast' and value == 'yes'\n   182\t            else:\n   183\t                rule, ok = 'a supported forecast or a justified unresolved answer', value == 'yes'\n   184\t            if not ok:\n   185\t                (splits if value == 'split' else fails).append(f'{pid} {item[\"label\"]}: {view} settled={value} [{rule}]')\n   186\t            lines.append(f'{pid} {item[\"label\"]:22} {view} {a[\"shape\"]:10} settled={value:6} votes={votes} [{rule}] {\"ok\" if ok else \"MISS\"}')\n   187\t    if need:\n   188\t        print('not final; needed:', ' | '.join(sorted(set(need))))\n   189\t        return\n   190\t    if floor_state in ('missed', 'rejected'):\n   191\t        fails.append(f'K-impossible-floor: the floor defect was {floor_state}')\n   192\t    elif floor_state == 'split':\n   193\t        splits.append('K-impossible-floor: the floor defect split')\n   194\t    verdict = 'fail' if fails else 'inconclusive' if splits else 'pass'\n   195\t    result = {'verdict': verdict, 'fails': fails, 'splits': splits, 'lines': lines, 'settled_defects': settled_defects,\n   196\t              'split_defects': split_defects, 'floor_control': floor_state}\n   197\t    (out / 'TALLY.json').write_text(json.dumps(result, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False))\n   198\t    print('\\n'.join(lines))\n   199\t    print('settled defects:', settled_defects)\n   200\t    print('split defects:', split_defects)\n   201\t    print('floor control:', floor_state)\n   202\t    print('fails:', fails)\n   203\t    print('splits:', splits)\n   204\t    print('VERDICT:', verdict)\n   205\t\n   206\t\n   207\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n   208\t    cmd = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) == 3 else ''\n   209\t    target = Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve() if len(sys.argv) == 3 else None\n   210\t    {'build': build, 'check': check, 'packets': packets, 'tally': tally}.get(\n   211\t        cmd, lambda _: (_ for _ in ()).throw(SystemExit(__doc__)))(target)\nBLIND5-RESULT.md\n     1\t# The D749 writer test of the E writer repair: result\n     2\t\n     3\tRun folder: `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/`. It was registered in `SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D749], with council round 64's\n     4\tchanges, and scored by `blind5.py tally` (`TALLY.json`, `reasons.json`). The request is `judging-v13s.txt`, sha256 `ac707fa9…`.\n     5\t\n     6\t## 1. Verdict: INCONCLUSIVE (two support splits, X05 and X08); no line failed\n     7\t\n     8\t**A correction, made after council round 65 (`codex-r65.md`).** I first recorded X08's two \"yes\" readings as compatible, although\n     9\tmy own note named the tension. The Claude reader read e1947 as a floor (\"at least $730B\") while accepting $710.4B. The Codex reader\n    10\tread it as a guide. Under the registered procedure, matching votes with incompatible reasons go to adjudication.\n    11\t- X08 was sent to adjudication. Both adjudicators said yes. The Claude adjudicator again read a floor above the outcome, and the\n    12\t  Codex adjudicator did not reconcile the $730B figure.\n    13\t- X08 is recorded as split (`reasons.json`). The row below is corrected, and the verdict stays INCONCLUSIVE.\n    14\t\n    15\t| Packet | Answer | Shape, rung | First readers (Codex, Claude) | Adjudicators (Codex, Claude) | Settled | Line |\n    16\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n    17\t| X06 | fresh E Codex | unresolved | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    18\t| X05 | fresh E Claude | forecast, rung 2 ($42B: 2.1x, 100% Vera) | no, yes | no, yes | split | inconclusive |\n    19\t| X02 | fresh S Codex | forecast, rung 4 ($730B estimate from the same four companies' AI-infrastructure plan) | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    20\t| X08 | fresh S Claude | forecast, rung 4 ($740B × 96% = $710.4B) | yes, yes (reasons incompatible: floor against guide) | yes, yes (reasons incompatible again) | split | inconclusive |\n    21\t| X01 | fresh P-v8 Claude | forecast, rung 2 ($383.9B) | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    22\t| X04 | fresh P-v8 Codex | forecast, rung 2 ($380.8B) | yes, yes | (none) | yes | ok |\n    23\t| X03 | control: invented 10% cut (blind4 U05) | forecast | no, no | (none) | no | ok |\n    24\t| X07 | control: impossible floor (blind4 U02) | forecast | floor marked by Codex only | floor upheld by both | floor settled | ok |\n    25\t\n    26\t- **The code** accepted all six fresh replies, and all six are publishable.\n    27\t- **No defect** was marked on a fresh reply.\n    28\t- **The reasons** behind the five settled fresh pairs and the two controls were read by Claude and recorded as compatible\n    29\t  (`reasons.json`). X08 is corrected to incompatible, as above.\n    30\t\n    31\t## 2. What changed against the targeted test (D745), same cases\n    32\t\n    33\t- **E.** The Codex writer no longer invents a cut. It answers unresolved and names the gap: both the FY2027 base and the FY2028\n    34\t  increase are projections, and no passage gives a shipment run-rate, an order with units and prices, or a deployment schedule. Both\n    35\t  readers accept it. In the targeted test, the same writer type cut the reference by 10% and was settled not supported.\n    36\t- **S.** Both fresh forecasts are supported by both families. In the targeted test both split.\n    37\t- **P-v8.** Both fresh replies are supported forecasts, as before. The repair did not cause withholding on the supported case.\n    38\t- **The controls.** Both read as expected.\n    39\t\n    40\t## 3. The one split, read against its passages (Claude's own trace reading)\n    41\t\n    42\t- **The answer.** E's Claude writer takes management's \"more than double\" in full, at 2.1x on $20B with Vera as 100%, giving $42B,\n    43\t  rung 2. It argues the FY2027 base \"is reaffirmed for the current year, so the CPU line is already selling at volume rather than a\n    44\t  product with no shipments\".\n    45\t- **The passages it saw (15).** None shows Vera shipments, reported Vera revenue or orders:\n    46\t  - e4689: \"will be deployed\";\n    47\t  - e5044: Anthropic \"is evaluating\";\n    48\t  - e4856: the $20B is a \"potential\";\n    49\t  - e3660: management \"still expects\" $20B, which is an outlook;\n    50\t  - the AMD benchmarks (e5399–e5404) show only that a Vera platform exists to be tested.\n    51\t- **The request's own rule** (bullet 2) says a target for a product with no shipments yet \"is taken in full only when the evidence\n    52\t  shows the volume in hand\".\n    53\t- **On the passages, the premise that decides this answer is not shown.**\n    54\t  - The Codex reader and the Codex adjudicator say so.\n    55\t  - The Claude adjudicator accepted the reaffirmed outlook and the benchmarked platform as enough.\n    56\t  - This is a question of fact against an existing rule, not a gap in Alex's D747 words. Where the families differ is whether a\n    57\t    reaffirmed outlook counts as \"volume in hand\".\n    58\t\n    59\t## 4. A trace note the readers did not mark (it became the X08 split after the correction)\n    60\t\n    61\t- **What the answer says.** S's Claude reply (X08) says data-center capex \"contains all AI capex plus non-AI cloud\n    62\t  capacity\". With e1947's more than $730B of AI infrastructure, that implies data-center capex above $730B, while its own outcome is\n    63\t  $710.4B.\n    64\t- **What it means.** The tension runs in the conservative direction and does not move the band (both figures are in rung 4).\n    65\t  Neither reader marked it. It is disclosed, not scored.\n    66\t\n    67\t## 5. Not done\n    68\t\n    69\tNothing was paid. Nothing was tuned on the 36 stored answers. The request was not changed after the registration.\ncodex-r65.md\n     1\t1. **Serious — INCONCLUSIVE is correct for the recorded votes. X05’s factual premise is resolvable.** NVIDIA saying it “still expects” $20B does not establish that Vera is already selling at volume. Across the 15 passages, deployments are prospective, Anthropic is evaluating the product, and AMD tested a platform. None reports sales or committed volume at the scale the answer assumes. X05 nevertheless treats doubling as a floor. Even granting its $42B forecast for all CPUs, Vera needs at least 95.2% of that total to reach $40B. The Vera-specific guidance makes $40B a relevant reference, but the answer never explains why a small miss is less likely. I would mark **this forecast unsupported** under the existing rule. That resolves the substance without changing the recorded split or ruling out a differently reasoned forecast. [E passages:9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/E/user.txt:9) · [X05 answer:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/E/answers/claude.json:1) · [Claude adjudication:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/adjudication/X05.claude.json:1) · [Codex adjudication:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/adjudication/X05.codex.json:5) · [Tally:12](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/TALLY.json:12)\n     2\t\n     3\t2. **Serious — Option 1 identifies the right distinction, but its closed list changes the rule in both directions.** An order with a delivery date can cover one unit. Reported sales to date can cover a pilot. Either meets Claude’s wording while leaving the scale of a full-year target open. Conversely, the request already permits a disclosed comparable scaled by capacity or units, and D747 permits an explained indirect comparison for a forecast. An exhaustive list could exclude evidence that establishes scale through those routes. The proposal names no company, but its list closely follows what was missing from E. The earlier writers invented a cut. X05 assumes full delivery. The recurring mistake is letting an unsupported assumption decide which side of the line wins. Section 1 calls for one rule at that level. Section 6 supplies no authority to invent an exhaustive list of acceptable documents. [Option 1:24](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r65.md:24) · [Discount and comparable instructions:4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [D745:11517](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11517) · [D747:11582](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11582) · [AGENTS §1:85](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:85) · [AGENTS §6:196](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/AGENTS.md:196)\n     4\t\n     5\t3. **Serious — X08 should have been flagged. Its two “yes” votes also required adjudication.** The source gives a *plan* above $730B. A $710.4B forecast can be coherent if the writer expects some planned spending to slip. But the Claude reader explicitly says data-center spending is **at least** $730B, then accepts $710.4B. The Codex reader calls $730B a **guide**, which permits a lower outcome. Those explanations disagree on whether the published number is possible. On Claude’s reading, the AI part exceeds the data-center whole by more than $19.6B, the existing defect illustrated by X07. Both numbers landing in the same band preserves the band choice but does nothing to reconcile the dollar figures. The registration sends matching votes with incompatible reasons to adjudication. X08 was recorded as compatible, so its support remains unverified. This is a missed review step, not a retrospectively settled failure. [S passage:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/S/user.txt:29) · [Writer’s inclusion claim:665](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/reader-packets/X08.md:665) · [Claude reading:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/reader-packets/X08.claude.json:1) · [Codex reading:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/reader-packets/X08.codex.json:5) · [Compatibility record:8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/reasons.json:8) · [Registration:472](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:472)\n     6\t\n     7\t4. **One recommendation.** Keep the paid re-send on hold. Use a smaller version of option 1 at bullet 2: *“A target remains a forecast when reaffirmed. To take it in full, show what evidence puts the required volume in hand for the period.”* This preserves the existing routes to a reasoned forecast or a justified “can’t tell.” Option 2 skips Alex’s clean-test condition. Option 3 asks Alex to decide whether an outlook reports sales, which the passages already settle. A further vote on unchanged X05 would leave the writer untouched. [Request:4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [Options 2 and 3:41](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/claude-r65.md:41) · [Alex’s authorization:11652](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11652)\n     8\t\n     9\t5. **One test.** After council review of that wording, register **one $0 blind writer test on the changed request** using D749’s E, S and P-v8 cases, one fresh writer from each family per case, and the original two controls. E must earn agreement on its forecast or its specific reason for withholding. S must earn agreement on reasoning consistent with its own dollar outcome: a reader citing a floor above that outcome cannot count as compatible with one citing a guide. Both P-v8 answers must remain supported forecasts. Keep the existing publication, defect and control conditions. An E-only pass would leave X08 unresolved and would not meet Alex’s three-case condition. **A clean pass supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send. A settled unsupported answer or defect fails. A persistent split stays inconclusive.** [D749 scope:11645](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11645) · [Pass and stop conditions:480](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:480)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba SMALL-DESIGN.md | tail -185; rg -n 'D750|D749|D747|D745' ../../CURRENT_STATE.md ../../DECISIONS.md\"","aggregated_output":"   352\t- **Request changes** (`judging-v13s.txt`; the v13 request is untouched, its plan hash is unchanged):\n   353\t  - \"If the chosen rung depends on a share, deduction or discount, show what in the passages supports its size or gives a bound that\n   354\t    justifies the rung. If the evidence cannot support a forecast, answer unresolved and explain the gap.\" This replaces the former\n   355\t    unresolved sentence.\n   356\t  - \"discounted by default\" becomes \"discounted subject to the evidence requirement below\".\n   357\t  - The qualifier list adds \"estimated\" (cases 111 of 111, mutants 43 of 43, rehearsal 19 of 19).\n   358\t- **Readers.** Shared rule text (`blind_rules.py`), including the allowed qualifier values and the unresolved ruling. First readers'\n   359\t  step 2 asks:\n   360\t  - for a forecast, the evidence for the band-deciding assumption;\n   361\t  - for an unresolved answer, the gap left after the strongest passages.\n   362\t  Adjudicators get the same definitions.\n   363\t- **Scope** (`blind4.py`; run folder `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23/`):\n   364\t  - cases S, E and P-v8;\n   365\t  - 6 unedited first replies (a fresh Claude subagent and a fresh read-only Codex session per case);\n   366\t  - 9 blinded packets (6 replies + 3 controls), each read by one Claude and one Codex reader: 18 first readings, plus adjudication\n   367\t    where they disagree.\n   368\t- **Controls**, each checked by the code before use:\n   369\t\n   370\t  | Control | Built from | Expected reading |\n   371\t  |---|---|---|\n   372\t  | K-unsupported | the saved third-run E Codex reply, with an unsized 15% cut | not supported |\n   373\t  | K-unresolved-unjustified | P-v8 Claude made unresolved with a vague reason | not supported |\n   374\t  | K-unresolved-justified | S made unresolved with the specific gap | supported |\n   375\t- **Pass:**\n   376\t  - every S and E reply has a settled \"yes\" on its forecast or on its reason for leaving the answer unresolved;\n   377\t  - both P-v8 replies have a settled \"yes\" on a forecast;\n   378\t  - all three controls read as expected;\n   379\t  - the refusal and defect stop lines hold as before.\n   380\t- **Otherwise:**\n   381\t  - a support split that adjudication does not settle leaves the run inconclusive, and it goes back to council;\n   382\t  - any failure goes back to council;\n   383\t  - a clean result supports asking Alex to authorize the 36-request paid re-send.\n   384\t\n   385\t**[D747] The re-read under Alex's comparison ruling (Alex: \"可以发布，要讲清楚\"; council rounds 61–61b), registered before any packet is\n   386\tbuilt.**\n   387\t- **The one change.** The shared definitions (`blind_rules.py`, \"supported\") add Alex's ruling. The band-deciding assumption must\n   388\t  rest on the passages in one of three ways:\n   389\t  - its size;\n   390\t  - a bound that justifies the rung;\n   391\t  - or, when the passages do not give the asked quantity, a related figure that the answer explains.\n   392\t\n   393\t  An explained related figure satisfies this even though the other side of the line remains possible. It is explained when the answer\n   394\t  says why the comparison applies to the companies, the period and the quantity asked, and why, under the answer's own stated\n   395\t  assumptions, the chosen side of the line is more likely. An answer that does not explain this is not supported.\n   396\t  - The first readers' step 2 asks, for a forecast, whether the passages support the deciding assumption's size or a bound, or whether\n   397\t    the answer explains a related figure as the definitions require.\n   398\t  - Adjudicators get the same definitions.\n   399\t  - The requests and the answers are unchanged. Each packet carries its writer's own request.\n   400\t- **What is re-read.** Nine stored answers under a fresh shuffle, W01–W09 (`blind4.py reread`). The key is in `reread-key.json`\n   401\t  beside, never in a packet.\n   402\t\n   403\t  | Answer | Expected reading |\n   404\t  |---|---|\n   405\t  | blind4 U01: P-v8, vague unresolved control | not supported |\n   406\t  | blind4 U02: S Claude, 98% share. It calls \"more than $730B\" a floor for data-center spending, then forecasts $705.6B of data-center spending on $720B of total spending, so its own assumptions cannot all hold (council 62) | not supported |\n   407\t  | blind4 U03: E, unsized 15% cut control | not supported |\n   408\t  | blind4 U05: E Codex, unsized 10% cut | not supported |\n   409\t  | blind3 T15: E Claude, a bracket between the market pace and the guidance, with Vera as all CPU revenue | supported |\n   410\t  | blind4 U08 (S Codex, $25B deduction) and U04 (S justified unresolved); blind3 T10 (S Claude, read for its spending argument only: its settled quotation error stands, and its defect marks are not scored); blind4 U06 (E Claude, 1.8x with a 90% Vera share, judged with its own share) | must settle either way: both first readers agree, or both adjudicators do |\n   411\t- **Changes from council round 62** (`codex-r62.md`), made before any packet was built:\n   412\t  - The definition says outright that an explained related figure satisfies the support requirement, even though the other side of\n   413\t    the line stays possible. Readers and adjudicators get the same words.\n   414\t  - Each packet carries the request its answer was written for. U03, T10 and T15 get the third run's request. The constructed\n   415\t    controls U01 and U04 are read under the request they were built for.\n   416\t  - The qualifier list shown comes from each packet's own schema, so the third run's packets do not list \"estimated\".\n   417\t  - All nine answers are shown in one layout, parsed and printed with one indent, so a control cannot be told apart by its layout.\n   418\t  - The tally refuses a key that is not exactly the nine answers, or a reading without a valid vote. A settled vote is final only\n   419\t    after Claude records its two reasons as compatible and applying Alex's rule (`reread-reasons.json`).\n   420\t    - Matching votes whose reasons are incompatible go to adjudication.\n   421\t    - An adjudicated agreement with incompatible reasons is a split.\n   422\t    - A \"yes\" on U06 that rests on the whole range staying at $30B or more does not apply the rule, since $20B × 1.5 × 90% = $27B.\n   423\t  - Checked on a scratch copy:\n   424\t    - without recorded reasons, the tally gives no verdict;\n   425\t    - with incompatible reasons, it asks for adjudication;\n   426\t    - with compatible reasons, it passes;\n   427\t    - a fixed \"no\" read as yes fails.\n   428\t- **Readers.** Fresh readers: one Claude subagent and one read-only Codex session per packet. Where they disagree, two adjudicators\n   429\t  read the packet, one per family.\n   430\t- **Scoring** (`blind4.py reread-tally`):\n   431\t  - It passes when the five fixed readings come out as expected and the four others settle.\n   432\t  - Matching votes whose stated reasons contradict each other on the comparison are recorded as unsettled. Claude reads them by hand.\n   433\t  - A settled defect on a writer's reply other than T10 is a stop.\n   434\t- **What the result decides:**\n   435\t  - Pass: the reading standard under D747 is settled. The next step is the E writer repair, with the council before any send, then a\n   436\t    $0 writer test, then Alex for the paid re-send.\n   437\t  - A split: Alex's words do not yet fix the reading. The split answers go back to the council, and to Alex as boundary cases.\n   438\t  - A failed fixed reading goes back to the council.\n   439\t  - A clean re-read does not turn D745 into a pass.\n   440\t\n   441\t**[D749] The $0 writer test of the E writer repair (Alex: \"批准修写手再小测\"; council round 63), registered before any writer is\n   442\tsent.**\n   443\t- **The request change** (`judging-v13s.txt`; the D745 text is kept in `judging-v13s-d745.txt`; the registered file's sha256 is\n   444\t  `ac707fa9…`, checked by `blind5.py build` against every built system text). This is the wording after council round 64\n   445\t  (`codex-r64.md`).\n   446\t  - The last bullet's two D745 sentences are replaced by: \"Before sizing a share, deduction, discount or pace that decides the band,\n   447\t    explain which band the evidence favours. Show support for the size or a justifying bound. If the passages lack the quantity asked,\n   448\t    explain why a related figure fits the companies, period and quantity, and why your assumptions favour that band. If you can say\n   449\t    only that the outcome might fall short or overshoot, not which band is more likely, answer unresolved and name what is unknown.\"\n   450\t  - Bullet 3's \"is an input to be discounted for time and execution (…), not an answer\" becomes \"is an input, not an answer: weigh\n   451\t    time and execution (…) under the evidence requirement below\". Council 64 found that the old imperative invited the old order\n   452\t    (discount first) on E.\n   453\t  - Sources:\n   454\t    - D745: show the support (council 64: \"give its size\" was narrower than D745, so \"show support for the size\");\n   455\t    - D747: an explained related figure counts, only when the passages lack the quantity asked (council 64: the first wording was\n   456\t      wider);\n   457\t    - D749: decide the band before sizing, else unresolved, naming the unknown;\n   458\t    - D745's ruling: a justified unresolved answer is usable.\n   459\t  - Size: 4,540 → 4,794 characters, 910 → 961 tokens (o200k_base). The writer's request now carries the same routes the readers judge\n   460\t    by, and the decision order Alex approved.\n   461\t  - Checks at $0: cases 111 of 111, rehearsal 19 of 19, and the pinned v13 plan unchanged (`paid-plan.sha256`). The schema and the code\n   462\t    are unchanged.\n   463\t- **Scope** (`blind5.py`; run folder `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/`):\n   464\t  - cases S, E and P-v8, built from the repaired request;\n   465\t  - one fresh Claude subagent and one fresh read-only Codex session per case, 6 writers, each reading only `system.txt`, `user.txt` and\n   466\t    `schema.json`.\n   467\t- **Readers.** 8 blinded packets, shuffled X01–X08, with the key in `reader-key.json`:\n   468\t  - the 6 fresh replies;\n   469\t  - 2 controls carried unchanged from the targeted test, each shown with the request it was written for;\n   470\t  - each packet read by one fresh Claude and one fresh Codex reader under the D747 definitions.\n   471\t\n   472\t  Where they disagree, on support or on any defect, two adjudicators read the packet, one per family. The reasons behind every\n   473\t  settled vote are recorded by Claude as compatible or not (`reasons.json`). Matching votes with incompatible reasons go to\n   474\t  adjudication.\n   475\t\n   476\t  | Control | Built from | Expected reading |\n   477\t  |---|---|---|\n   478\t  | K-invented-cut | blind4 U05, E Codex: 90% of $40B with no order size or shipment pace | not supported |\n   479\t  | K-impossible-floor | blind4 U02, S Claude: \"more than $730B\" called a floor above its own $720B total | \"part above or added into its whole\" on F12, settled; its support is not scored |\n   480\t- **Pass:**\n   481\t  - every fresh S and E reply has a settled yes, on its forecast or on its unresolved reason;\n   482\t  - both fresh P-v8 replies have a settled yes on a forecast;\n   483\t  - every fresh reply is accepted and publishable by the code;\n   484\t  - no settled defect on a fresh reply;\n   485\t  - both controls read as expected.\n   486\t- **Otherwise (tally rules after council 64):**\n   487\t  - **Fail:**\n   488\t    - a fresh reply refused or held by the code (decided before any reading; an unreadable reply builds no packet);\n   489\t    - a fresh P-v8 reply that is not a forecast (decided from its shape alone);\n   490\t    - a settled no on a fresh reply;\n   491\t    - a settled defect on a fresh reply;\n   492\t    - K-invented-cut not settled no;\n   493\t    - the floor defect marked by neither reader, or rejected by both adjudicators.\n   494\t  - **Inconclusive:** a support split, a defect split on a fresh reply, or a floor split left after adjudication.\n   495\t  - **The floor control** is matched on its type and on naming F12, at both stages, so readers who list the other figures differently\n   496\t    still agree. Adjudicator votes are validated like first votes.\n   497\t  - Either outcome goes back to the council, and the paid re-send stays on hold.\n   498\t  - Only a clean pass supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send.\n   499\t- **Checked on a scratch copy before the send** (the targeted test's six replies stood in as fresh replies):\n   500\t  - a clean set passes, with the floor marked by readers who listed its figures differently;\n   501\t  - a fresh defect marked by one reader waits for adjudication;\n   502\t  - a fresh defect still split after adjudication is inconclusive;\n   503\t  - the invented-cut control read as supported fails;\n   504\t  - the floor missed by both readers fails;\n   505\t  - a fresh P-v8 answered unresolved fails;\n   506\t  - a fresh reply that is not JSON fails before any reading.\n   507\t- **Known limits, disclosed now:**\n   508\t  - Readers split on boundary answers (D748). A fresh answer on a boundary can leave the run inconclusive even when the repair works.\n   509\t  - All four fresh E and S replies may pass as justified \"unresolved\". A pass therefore shows the repair stops invented sizes. It\n   510\t    does not show how often the writer withholds on boundary cases (council 64).\n   511\t\n   512\t**[D750] The second $0 writer test (council round 65; under D439 while Alex is away), registered before any writer is sent.**\n   513\t- **Why.** The D749 test was INCONCLUSIVE, with no failed line (`BLIND5-RESULT.md`).\n   514\t  - X05, E Claude, took a not-yet-shipping target in full, asserting \"already selling at volume\". None of E's 15 passages shows\n   515\t    shipments, revenue to date or orders.\n   516\t  - X08, S Claude: its readers disagreed on whether \"more than $730B\" of AI infrastructure is a floor above its own $710.4B outcome.\n   517\t- **The request change** (`judging-v13s.txt`; the D749 text is kept in `judging-v13s-d749.txt`; the registered sha256 `54f5847d…` is\n   518\t  checked by `blind6.py build` against every built system text). Bullet 2's \"it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the\n   519\t  volume in hand\" becomes \"it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence puts the\n   520\t  required volume in hand for the period\".\n   521\t  - This is council 65's wording. Claude's closed list was rejected: an order with a date can cover one unit, and a list would\n   522\t    exclude the request's own disclosed-comparable route and D747's explained comparison.\n   523\t  - Size: 4,794 → 4,867 characters, 961 → 975 tokens.\n   524\t  - Checks: cases 111 of 111, rehearsal 19 of 19, and the pinned v13 plan unchanged.\n   525\t- **Design.** D749's, unchanged (`blind6.py` wraps `blind5.py`), on a new run folder, `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/`:\n   526\t  - S, E and P-v8, each with one fresh Claude and one fresh read-only Codex writer;\n   527\t  - the same two reader controls (K-invented-cut, K-impossible-floor);\n   528\t  - fresh readers of both families, with adjudication where they disagree;\n   529\t  - the same pass, fail and inconclusive lines.\n   530\t- **One added reading rule** for the reasons record (council 65), applied by Claude before any vote counts as settled. On S, a reader\n   531\t  citing a related figure as a floor above the answer's own outcome is not compatible with a reader treating it as a guide. Such a\n   532\t  pair goes to adjudication.\n   533\t- **What the result decides:**\n   534\t  - a clean pass supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send;\n   535\t  - a settled unsupported answer or defect fails;\n   536\t  - a persistent split stays inconclusive and goes back to the council.\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:448:**The one next task: the $0 writer test of the E writer repair (D749), after council round 64 reviews the request change.** Alex\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:451:- **The repair** (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt` line 9; the D745 text is kept in `judging-v13s-d745.txt`).\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:456:- **The test** is registered in `SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D749] and built by `blind5.py`:\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:463:**Earlier next task (done, D749): Alex chooses whether to authorize the E writer repair (D748).**\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:465:- **Why.** The re-read under his comparison ruling (D747) failed on a stop (`research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md` §6).\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:476:The record of the D747 step:\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:478:**Earlier next task (done, D748): the $0 blinded re-read under Alex's comparison ruling (D747), after council round 62 reviews it.** Alex ruled\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:479:(D747: publish, with the reason explained) that a forecast may rest on a related figure when the passages do not give the asked quantity. It is\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:484:- The re-read is registered in `SMALL-DESIGN.md` §5 [D747]: nine stored answers, four fixed readings and five that must settle.\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:487:The record of the D746 step (Alex answered its question in D747):\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:489:**Earlier next task (done, D747): Alex answers one general question (D746).** \"When the passages do not give the asked number, and\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:504:The record of the D745 step:\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:506:**Earlier next task (done, D746): Alex chooses whether to authorize a targeted $0 test (D745).** The test covered:\n../../CURRENT_STATE.md:523:**Earlier next task (done, D745): Alex chooses whether to authorize one more bounded blinded re-read (D744).**\n../../DECISIONS.md:1089:| D745 | 2026-11-23 | D744 re-read: readers calibrated (5/5 controls, no shared false mark); STOP on a qualifier-list gap (\"an estimated\" forced to none) and on S zero usable (unsupported data-center share decides the band; E's 15% cut the same); council 59: targeted $0 test of one clarification (show evidence or a supported bound for a band-deciding deduction, else unresolved) plus the qualifier fix; Alex: \"批准针对性小测\", and a justified unresolved answer counts as usable (\"算合格\") | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND3-RESULT.md` |\n../../DECISIONS.md:1090:| D746 | 2026-11-23 | D745 targeted test FAILS: E's Codex reply settled not supported (an unsized 10% cut decides the band); S's two replies, E's Claude reply and the justified-unresolved control split along model family (8 of 8 adjudicator votes); P-v8 2 of 2; 0 of 6 withheld; council 61–61b: ask Alex one general question (may a forecast rest on an explained indirect comparison, or must it wait until the passages settle the deciding side; lean: allow it, explained), then one $0 blinded re-read of nine stored answers under his words; the paid re-send stays on hold until an E writer repair passes a clean $0 test; question answered in D747 | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md` |\n../../DECISIONS.md:1091:| D747 | 2026-11-23 | Alex: \"可以发布，要讲清楚\" — a forecast may rest on a related figure when the passages do not give the asked quantity, supported only when the answer explains why the comparison applies to the companies, period and quantity asked and why, under its own stated assumptions, that side of the line is more likely; D741 ruling 3 and D745's unresolved ruling still hold; next: the words into the shared reader definitions, then one $0 blinded re-read of nine stored answers after council review | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n../../DECISIONS.md:1092:| D748 | 2026-11-23 | D747 re-read FAILS on a stop: U02 (S Claude) calls \"more than $730B\" a floor above its own $720B total, both adjudicators upheld part-above-whole (code cannot see a prose floor; 1 of 18 stored replies); 6 of 9 settle with compatible reasons, 3 of 4 earlier splits settle (U04 yes, U06 no, U08 yes); T10, T15, U02 support still split (adjudicators follow family, stricter family changes by question); process error: uncalibrated \"must settle\" conjunction; council 63: no further reader round; ask Alex to authorize the E writer repair (decide the side before any discount; else say what is unknown), then one $0 writer test on E, S, P-v8 with U05 and U02 as controls; format change deferred; paid re-send on hold | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND4-RESULT.md` |\n../../DECISIONS.md:1093:| D749 | 2026-11-23 | Alex: \"批准修写手再小测\" — repair the writer request (decide which side of the line the evidence favours before any discount; else \"can't tell\" naming what is missing), council review before any send, then one $0 blind writer test on E, S and P-v8 with saved U05 and U02 as reader controls under D748's lines; paid re-send on hold until it passes clean | in force | `docs/DECISIONS-log.md` |\n../../DECISIONS.md:1094:| D750 | 2026-11-23 | D749 writer test INCONCLUSIVE, no failed line: E Codex now withholds with a specific gap (both accept), both P-v8 and S Codex supported, both controls caught; splits on X05 (E Claude takes a not-yet-shipping target in full; no passage shows volume in hand) and X08 (S Claude, floor vs guide reading; my compatibility record corrected after council 65); council 65 under D439 (Alex asleep, \"自行收敛\"): bullet 2 \"it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence puts the required volume in hand for the period\", closed list rejected; second $0 writer test on S, E, P-v8 with the same controls and lines; paid re-send on hold | in force | `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/BLIND5-RESULT.md` |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba judging-v13s.txt && diff -u judging-v13s-d749.txt judging-v13s.txt\nnl -ba blind6.py\nnl -ba blind5.py | head -102\nnl -ba SMALL-DESIGN.md | tail -91'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && nl -ba judging-v13s.txt && diff -u judging-v13s-d749.txt judging-v13s.txt\nnl -ba blind6.py\nnl -ba blind5.py | head -102\nnl -ba SMALL-DESIGN.md | tail -91'","aggregated_output":"     1\tYou are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n     2\t\n     3\t- Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\n     4\t- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate whose pace you forecast, informed by guidance, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted subject to the evidence requirement below; it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence puts the required volume in hand for the period. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n     5\t- Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input, not an answer: weigh time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say) under the evidence requirement below; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n     6\t- An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n     7\t- \"Themes in force\" lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on a member and report it in that member's theme_pushes with the direction it pushes that member (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \"updated since this thesis was last judged\" may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     8\t- Your conclusions must be consistent with each other and with the themes in force as shown: a share cannot be judged at zero while the policy that gates it is judged likely to open.\n     9\t- Return the family's figures and one answer per member, as the JSON schema defines them. Every number an answer rests on is a figure; a number you judge rather than read or compute is an estimate, stated as yours. Before sizing a share, deduction, discount or pace that decides the band, explain which band the evidence favours. Show support for the size or a justifying bound. If the passages lack the quantity asked, explain why a related figure fits the companies, period and quantity, and why your assumptions favour that band. If you can say only that the outcome might fall short or overshoot, not which band is more likely, answer unresolved and name what is unknown. Write explanations in English; preserve IDs and any quoted source text.\n--- judging-v13s-d749.txt\t2026-11-23 01:13:45\n+++ judging-v13s.txt\t2026-11-23 01:13:52\n@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@\n You are a senior hedge-fund analyst judging the current rungs of a family of related number theses: one company's quantities that overlap, such as a total and its segment, a level and its growth, or a later year that rests on an earlier year's base. Use only the supplied evidence and themes in force. Each rung is your forecast: the outcome the evidence in force makes most likely at the due date, not the one it has proved.\n \n - Judge every member from the evidence shown (what recent judgements relied on and what arrived recently) and the themes in force, as if for the first time. Earlier forecasts are not shown: whether a conclusion changed is compared afterwards.\n-- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate whose pace you forecast, informed by guidance, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted subject to the evidence requirement below; it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the volume in hand. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n+- Judge each member against a reference: what the market expects for that question (consensus, the company's guidance, the stated plan or deadline). Say where the reference sits on its ladder. A consensus or guidance figure by itself keeps the judgement at the reference's rung; once other evidence has arrived it is never the reason to stay. Then derive the outcome the evidence implies: reported figures and guidance give a run-rate whose pace you forecast, informed by guidance, never the last quarter annualised flat; a quantified revision, a customer's demand number, a supplier's constraint, a confirmed delay or cancellation shift it. A target for a product with no shipments yet is discounted subject to the evidence requirement below; it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence puts the required volume in hand for the period. Build the family's figures once and read every member's outcome from them: a part cannot exceed its whole, a figure that spans several periods or products gives a question only its share, and a quantity the family shares has one forecast. Compare each outcome with its rung boundaries, and move when it crosses one.\n - Weigh by tier and by novelty. Only fact can establish that a rung's outcome already holds; \"not established\" is a statement of confidence, never a reason to stay. Guidance for the current or next quarter is the strongest forecast input. A management target for a product not yet shipping, or an ambition spanning years, is an input, not an answer: weigh time and execution (how many selling quarters remain, what volume and price the figure implies, what the company's own choices say) under the evidence requirement below; consensus is where the market stands, not the answer either. third_party_view and rumour move the forecast in proportion to their specificity (a number, a date, a named party): a research firm's shipment or revenue tracking with a number counts. A commitment or deal that is announced but not sized is sized from its disclosed comparable (the same programme's other deal, scaled by capacity or units); a figure no one states is derived from the accounting identities in the evidence when they allow it. A repeat, another outlet for the same claim, or an opinion that adds no new fact or calculation moves nothing. Missing confirmation alone is not grounds for the lowest or highest rung: an event not being confirmed is not confirmation that it did not happen.\n - An evidence item that replaces another includes its predecessor for context, such as guidance revised from 12% to 25% growth. The predecessor is no longer evidence in force.\n - \"Themes in force\" lists the library's open theme theses (policy stages, shared quantities) with their current conclusions. They are our own judgements, never evidence: do not cite them in cites. Weigh each one that bears on a member and report it in that member's theme_pushes with the direction it pushes that member (toward_first, toward_last or none); leave out a theme that does not bear on it. A theme marked \"updated since this thesis was last judged\" may change the conclusion; one that is not marked already stood at the previous judgement. When no themes are listed, theme_pushes is empty.\n     1\t\"\"\"The D750 $0 writer test (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5 [D750]): blind5's design, unchanged, on the request with council 65's bullet-2 sentence\n     2\t(\"it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence puts the required volume in hand for the\n     3\tperiod\"). Cases S, E and P-v8; a fresh Claude and Codex writer each; the same two reader controls; the same tally.\n     4\t\n     5\t  python3 blind6.py build|check|packets|tally <out>\n     6\t\"\"\"\n     7\timport sys\n     8\tfrom pathlib import Path\n     9\t\n    10\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    11\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    12\timport blind5  # noqa: E402\n    13\t\n    14\tblind5.REQUEST_SHA256 = '54f5847d715caec159e6509b7966c13df4d4af0756953d206fefa1347879f397'   # judging-v13s.txt as registered (D750)\n    15\tblind5.READER_BRIEF = blind5.READER_BRIEF.replace('writer test, D749', 'writer test, D750')\n    16\tif 'D750' not in blind5.READER_BRIEF:\n    17\t    raise SystemExit('the D750 reader brief is not built')\n    18\t\n    19\tif __name__ == '__main__':\n    20\t    cmd = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) == 3 else ''\n    21\t    target = Path(sys.argv[2]).resolve() if len(sys.argv) == 3 else None\n    22\t    {'build': blind5.build, 'check': blind5.check, 'packets': blind5.packets, 'tally': blind5.tally}.get(\n    23\t        cmd, lambda _: (_ for _ in ()).throw(SystemExit(__doc__)))(target)\n     1\t\"\"\"The D749 $0 writer test (SMALL-DESIGN.md §5 [D749]): cases S, E and P-v8 built from the repaired request (judging-v13s.txt, the\n     2\t\"decide the side before you size it\" sentence), a fresh Claude and Codex writer each, readers under the D747 definitions, and two\n     3\treader controls carried from the targeted test with the request they were written for: U05 (E Codex, an invented 10% cut; expected\n     4\tnot supported) and U02 (S Claude, a floor above its own total; expected the part-above-whole defect upheld).\n     5\t\n     6\t  python3 blind5.py build <out>      # the three requests and writer prompts (refuses an existing folder)\n     7\t  python3 blind5.py check <out>      # every first answer through the schema, from_answer, check and publish_decision\n     8\t  python3 blind5.py packets <out>    # 6 replies + 2 controls, shuffled X01–X08; key beside\n     9\t  python3 blind5.py tally <out>      # the registered lines, after readings, recorded reasons and any adjudication\n    10\t\"\"\"\n    11\timport hashlib\n    12\timport json\n    13\timport random\n    14\timport sys\n    15\tfrom pathlib import Path\n    16\t\n    17\tHERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\n    18\tsys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))\n    19\timport blind4 as b4  # noqa: E402\n    20\tfrom blind_rules import format_material  # noqa: E402\n    21\t\n    22\tCASES = b4.CASES                                                     # ('S', 'E', 'P-v8')\n    23\tBLIND4 = HERE.parents[2] / 'poc/data/judging-v13s-blind4-2026-11-23'\n    24\tCONTROLS = {'K-invented-cut': ('E', 'codex'), 'K-impossible-floor': ('S', 'claude')}     # blind4 U05 and U02, unchanged\n    25\tFLOOR_DEFECT = ('part above or added into its whole', ('F11', 'F12', 'F15'))\n    26\tREADER_BRIEF = b4.REREAD_BRIEF.replace('re-read under the comparison ruling, D747', 'writer test, D749')\n    27\tREQUEST_SHA256 = 'ac707fa96890cee1f69dcf84e6c5242ec014b00b502214ece84b1318252a9859'   # judging-v13s.txt as registered (council 64)\n    28\tif 'D749' not in READER_BRIEF:\n    29\t    raise SystemExit('the D749 reader brief is not built')\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\tdef build(out):\n    33\t    request = (HERE / 'judging-v13s.txt').read_bytes()\n    34\t    if hashlib.sha256(request).hexdigest() != REQUEST_SHA256:\n    35\t        raise SystemExit('judging-v13s.txt is not the registered D749 request')\n    36\t    b4.build(out)\n    37\t    for name in CASES:\n    38\t        if (out / name / 'system.txt').read_bytes() != request:\n    39\t            raise SystemExit(f'{name}: the built system text is not the registered D749 request')\n    40\t\n    41\t\n    42\tdef check(out):\n    43\t    b4.check(out)\n    44\t\n    45\t\n    46\tdef packets(out):\n    47\t    rows = json.loads((out / 'CHECKED.json').read_text())\n    48\t    unreadable = [f'{r[\"case\"]}/{r[\"writer\"]} ({r[\"stage\"]})' for r in rows if r['stage'] != 'checked']\n    49\t    if unreadable:      # a reply refused before the checks has no answer to read; the run has already failed (registered)\n    50\t        print('FAIL: first replies refused before the code checks:', ', '.join(unreadable), '- readers are not needed for the verdict')\n    51\t    items = [{'label': f'fresh {r[\"case\"]}/{r[\"writer\"]}', 'case': r['case'], 'writer': r['writer'],\n    52\t              'answer': str(out / r['case'] / 'answers' / f'{r[\"writer\"]}.json'), 'case_dir': str(out / r['case'])}\n    53\t             for r in rows if r['stage'] == 'checked']\n    54\t    for name, (case, writer) in CONTROLS.items():\n    55\t        items.append({'label': name, 'case': case, 'writer': name, 'answer': str(BLIND4 / case / 'answers' / f'{writer}.json'),\n    56\t                      'case_dir': str(BLIND4 / case)})\n    57\t    order = list(range(len(items)))\n    58\t    random.Random(hashlib.sha256(b'D749 ' + (out / 'CHECKED.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest()).shuffle(order)\n    59\t    folder = out / 'reader-packets'\n    60\t    folder.mkdir(exist_ok=False)\n    61\t    key = {}\n    62\t    for n, i in enumerate(order, 1):\n    63\t        item = items[i]\n    64\t        case_dir = Path(item['case_dir'])\n    65\t        pid = f'X{n:02d}'\n    66\t        key[pid] = item\n    67\t        (folder / f'{pid}.md').write_text('\\n'.join([READER_BRIEF, format_material(case_dir), '', '# The request as the writer saw it', '',\n    68\t                                                     (case_dir / 'user.txt').read_text(), '', '# The answer', '',\n    69\t                                                     b4._display(item['answer']), '']))\n    70\t        (folder / f'{pid}.codex-prompt.txt').write_text(\n    71\t            f'Read the file {folder / f\"{pid}.md\"} and nothing else (no other file, no web). Follow the brief at its top: read the request '\n    72\t            'and the answer it contains, and return only the JSON the brief asks for, with no text before or after it.\\n')\n    73\t    (out / 'reader-key.json').write_text(json.dumps(key, indent=1))\n    74\t    print(f'{len(order)} packets in {folder}; key in reader-key.json (keep from readers)')\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\tdef _keys(reading, floor):\n    78\t    \"\"\"A reading's defect keys; on the floor control, every part-above-whole mark naming F12 is one key (council 64).\"\"\"\n    79\t    keys = set()\n    80\t    for d in reading.get('defects', []):\n    81\t        k = b4._defect_key(d)\n    82\t        keys.add((FLOOR_DEFECT[0], ('F12',)) if floor and k[0] == FLOOR_DEFECT[0] and 'F12' in k[1] else k)\n    83\t    return keys\n    84\t\n    85\t\n    86\tdef _decisions(reading, floor):\n    87\t    found = {}\n    88\t    for d in reading.get('defects', []):\n    89\t        k = b4._defect_key(d)\n    90\t        k = (FLOOR_DEFECT[0], ('F12',)) if floor and k[0] == FLOOR_DEFECT[0] and 'F12' in k[1] else k\n    91\t        if found.get(k) != 'uphold':          # a key both listed as upheld and as rejected counts as upheld only if upheld once\n    92\t            found[k] = d.get('decision')\n    93\t    return found\n    94\t\n    95\t\n    96\tdef _vote(value, where):\n    97\t    if value not in ('yes', 'no'):\n    98\t        raise SystemExit(f'{where}: no valid vote ({value!r})')\n    99\t    return value\n   100\t\n   101\t\n   102\tdef tally(out):\n   446\t  - The last bullet's two D745 sentences are replaced by: \"Before sizing a share, deduction, discount or pace that decides the band,\n   447\t    explain which band the evidence favours. Show support for the size or a justifying bound. If the passages lack the quantity asked,\n   448\t    explain why a related figure fits the companies, period and quantity, and why your assumptions favour that band. If you can say\n   449\t    only that the outcome might fall short or overshoot, not which band is more likely, answer unresolved and name what is unknown.\"\n   450\t  - Bullet 3's \"is an input to be discounted for time and execution (…), not an answer\" becomes \"is an input, not an answer: weigh\n   451\t    time and execution (…) under the evidence requirement below\". Council 64 found that the old imperative invited the old order\n   452\t    (discount first) on E.\n   453\t  - Sources:\n   454\t    - D745: show the support (council 64: \"give its size\" was narrower than D745, so \"show support for the size\");\n   455\t    - D747: an explained related figure counts, only when the passages lack the quantity asked (council 64: the first wording was\n   456\t      wider);\n   457\t    - D749: decide the band before sizing, else unresolved, naming the unknown;\n   458\t    - D745's ruling: a justified unresolved answer is usable.\n   459\t  - Size: 4,540 → 4,794 characters, 910 → 961 tokens (o200k_base). The writer's request now carries the same routes the readers judge\n   460\t    by, and the decision order Alex approved.\n   461\t  - Checks at $0: cases 111 of 111, rehearsal 19 of 19, and the pinned v13 plan unchanged (`paid-plan.sha256`). The schema and the code\n   462\t    are unchanged.\n   463\t- **Scope** (`blind5.py`; run folder `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/`):\n   464\t  - cases S, E and P-v8, built from the repaired request;\n   465\t  - one fresh Claude subagent and one fresh read-only Codex session per case, 6 writers, each reading only `system.txt`, `user.txt` and\n   466\t    `schema.json`.\n   467\t- **Readers.** 8 blinded packets, shuffled X01–X08, with the key in `reader-key.json`:\n   468\t  - the 6 fresh replies;\n   469\t  - 2 controls carried unchanged from the targeted test, each shown with the request it was written for;\n   470\t  - each packet read by one fresh Claude and one fresh Codex reader under the D747 definitions.\n   471\t\n   472\t  Where they disagree, on support or on any defect, two adjudicators read the packet, one per family. The reasons behind every\n   473\t  settled vote are recorded by Claude as compatible or not (`reasons.json`). Matching votes with incompatible reasons go to\n   474\t  adjudication.\n   475\t\n   476\t  | Control | Built from | Expected reading |\n   477\t  |---|---|---|\n   478\t  | K-invented-cut | blind4 U05, E Codex: 90% of $40B with no order size or shipment pace | not supported |\n   479\t  | K-impossible-floor | blind4 U02, S Claude: \"more than $730B\" called a floor above its own $720B total | \"part above or added into its whole\" on F12, settled; its support is not scored |\n   480\t- **Pass:**\n   481\t  - every fresh S and E reply has a settled yes, on its forecast or on its unresolved reason;\n   482\t  - both fresh P-v8 replies have a settled yes on a forecast;\n   483\t  - every fresh reply is accepted and publishable by the code;\n   484\t  - no settled defect on a fresh reply;\n   485\t  - both controls read as expected.\n   486\t- **Otherwise (tally rules after council 64):**\n   487\t  - **Fail:**\n   488\t    - a fresh reply refused or held by the code (decided before any reading; an unreadable reply builds no packet);\n   489\t    - a fresh P-v8 reply that is not a forecast (decided from its shape alone);\n   490\t    - a settled no on a fresh reply;\n   491\t    - a settled defect on a fresh reply;\n   492\t    - K-invented-cut not settled no;\n   493\t    - the floor defect marked by neither reader, or rejected by both adjudicators.\n   494\t  - **Inconclusive:** a support split, a defect split on a fresh reply, or a floor split left after adjudication.\n   495\t  - **The floor control** is matched on its type and on naming F12, at both stages, so readers who list the other figures differently\n   496\t    still agree. Adjudicator votes are validated like first votes.\n   497\t  - Either outcome goes back to the council, and the paid re-send stays on hold.\n   498\t  - Only a clean pass supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send.\n   499\t- **Checked on a scratch copy before the send** (the targeted test's six replies stood in as fresh replies):\n   500\t  - a clean set passes, with the floor marked by readers who listed its figures differently;\n   501\t  - a fresh defect marked by one reader waits for adjudication;\n   502\t  - a fresh defect still split after adjudication is inconclusive;\n   503\t  - the invented-cut control read as supported fails;\n   504\t  - the floor missed by both readers fails;\n   505\t  - a fresh P-v8 answered unresolved fails;\n   506\t  - a fresh reply that is not JSON fails before any reading.\n   507\t- **Known limits, disclosed now:**\n   508\t  - Readers split on boundary answers (D748). A fresh answer on a boundary can leave the run inconclusive even when the repair works.\n   509\t  - All four fresh E and S replies may pass as justified \"unresolved\". A pass therefore shows the repair stops invented sizes. It\n   510\t    does not show how often the writer withholds on boundary cases (council 64).\n   511\t\n   512\t**[D750] The second $0 writer test (council round 65; under D439 while Alex is away), registered before any writer is sent.**\n   513\t- **Why.** The D749 test was INCONCLUSIVE, with no failed line (`BLIND5-RESULT.md`).\n   514\t  - X05, E Claude, took a not-yet-shipping target in full, asserting \"already selling at volume\". None of E's 15 passages shows\n   515\t    shipments, revenue to date or orders.\n   516\t  - X08, S Claude: its readers disagreed on whether \"more than $730B\" of AI infrastructure is a floor above its own $710.4B outcome.\n   517\t- **The request change** (`judging-v13s.txt`; the D749 text is kept in `judging-v13s-d749.txt`; the registered sha256 `54f5847d…` is\n   518\t  checked by `blind6.py build` against every built system text). Bullet 2's \"it is taken in full only when the evidence shows the\n   519\t  volume in hand\" becomes \"it remains a forecast when reaffirmed, and is taken in full only when you show what evidence puts the\n   520\t  required volume in hand for the period\".\n   521\t  - This is council 65's wording. Claude's closed list was rejected: an order with a date can cover one unit, and a list would\n   522\t    exclude the request's own disclosed-comparable route and D747's explained comparison.\n   523\t  - Size: 4,794 → 4,867 characters, 961 → 975 tokens.\n   524\t  - Checks: cases 111 of 111, rehearsal 19 of 19, and the pinned v13 plan unchanged.\n   525\t- **Design.** D749's, unchanged (`blind6.py` wraps `blind5.py`), on a new run folder, `poc/data/judging-v13s-blind6-2026-11-23/`:\n   526\t  - S, E and P-v8, each with one fresh Claude and one fresh read-only Codex writer;\n   527\t  - the same two reader controls (K-invented-cut, K-impossible-floor);\n   528\t  - fresh readers of both families, with adjudication where they disagree;\n   529\t  - the same pass, fail and inconclusive lines.\n   530\t- **One added reading rule** for the reasons record (council 65), applied by Claude before any vote counts as settled. On S, a reader\n   531\t  citing a related figure as a floor above the answer's own outcome is not compatible with a reader treating it as a guide. Such a\n   532\t  pair goes to adjudication.\n   533\t- **What the result decides:**\n   534\t  - a clean pass supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send;\n   535\t  - a settled unsupported answer or defect fails;\n   536\t  - a persistent split stays inconclusive and goes back to the council.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
