{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && python3 -B -c 'import blind6, json, io\nfrom contextlib import redirect_stdout\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nfrom pathlib import Path\nb=blind6.blind5\nout=b.BLIND4.parent/\\\"judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23\\\"\norig=Path.read_text\norig_exists=Path.exists\nfor mode in (\\\"paired identical reasons\\\", \\\"split invented-cut control\\\", \\\"missing floor decision\\\"):\n    def read(path,*args,**kwargs):\n        if path.name==\\\"reasons.json\\\":\n            data=json.loads(orig(path))\n            for pid in (\\\"X05\\\",\\\"X08\\\"):\n                data[pid]={\\\"first\\\":\\\"compatible\\\"}\n            return json.dumps(data)\n        if path.parent.name==\\\"reader-packets\\\" and path.name in (\\\"X05.codex.json\\\",\\\"X08.codex.json\\\"):\n            return orig(path.with_suffix(\\\"\\\").with_suffix(\\\".claude.json\\\"))\n        if mode.startswith(\\\"split\\\") and path.name==\\\"X03.codex.json\\\":\n            return json.dumps({\\\"members\\\":{\\\"v41\\\":{\\\"supported\\\":\\\"yes\\\"}},\\\"defects\\\":[]})\n        if mode.startswith(\\\"split\\\") and path.parent.name==\\\"adjudication\\\" and path.name==\\\"X03.claude.json\\\":\n            return json.dumps({\\\"members\\\":{\\\"v41\\\":{\\\"supported\\\":\\\"no\\\"}},\\\"defects\\\":[]})\n        if mode.startswith(\\\"missing\\\") and path.parent.name==\\\"adjudication\\\" and path.name==\\\"X07.codex.json\\\":\n            data=json.loads(orig(path))\n            data[\\\"defects\\\"]=[]\n            return json.dumps(data)\n        return orig(path,*args,**kwargs)\n    def exists(path):\n        return orig_exists(path) or (mode.startswith(\\\"split\\\") and path.parent.name==\\\"adjudication\\\" and path.name.startswith(\\\"X03.\\\"))\n    buffer=io.StringIO()\n    with patch.object(Path,\\\"read_text\\\",read),patch.object(Path,\\\"exists\\\",exists),patch.object(Path,\\\"write_text\\\") as write,redirect_stdout(buffer):\n        b.tally(out)\n    result=json.loads(write.call_args.args[0])\n    print(mode,result[\\\"verdict\\\"],result[\\\"fails\\\"],result[\\\"splits\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"cd docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers && python3 -B -c 'import blind6, json, io\nfrom contextlib import redirect_stdout\nfrom unittest.mock import patch\nfrom pathlib import Path\nb=blind6.blind5\nout=b.BLIND4.parent/\\\"judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23\\\"\norig=Path.read_text\norig_exists=Path.exists\nfor mode in (\\\"paired identical reasons\\\", \\\"split invented-cut control\\\", \\\"missing floor decision\\\"):\n    def read(path,*args,**kwargs):\n        if path.name==\\\"reasons.json\\\":\n            data=json.loads(orig(path))\n            for pid in (\\\"X05\\\",\\\"X08\\\"):\n                data[pid]={\\\"first\\\":\\\"compatible\\\"}\n            return json.dumps(data)\n        if path.parent.name==\\\"reader-packets\\\" and path.name in (\\\"X05.codex.json\\\",\\\"X08.codex.json\\\"):\n            return orig(path.with_suffix(\\\"\\\").with_suffix(\\\".claude.json\\\"))\n        if mode.startswith(\\\"split\\\") and path.name==\\\"X03.codex.json\\\":\n            return json.dumps({\\\"members\\\":{\\\"v41\\\":{\\\"supported\\\":\\\"yes\\\"}},\\\"defects\\\":[]})\n        if mode.startswith(\\\"split\\\") and path.parent.name==\\\"adjudication\\\" and path.name==\\\"X03.claude.json\\\":\n            return json.dumps({\\\"members\\\":{\\\"v41\\\":{\\\"supported\\\":\\\"no\\\"}},\\\"defects\\\":[]})\n        if mode.startswith(\\\"missing\\\") and path.parent.name==\\\"adjudication\\\" and path.name==\\\"X07.codex.json\\\":\n            data=json.loads(orig(path))\n            data[\\\"defects\\\"]=[]\n            return json.dumps(data)\n        return orig(path,*args,**kwargs)\n    def exists(path):\n        return orig_exists(path) or (mode.startswith(\\\"split\\\") and path.parent.name==\\\"adjudication\\\" and path.name.startswith(\\\"X03.\\\"))\n    buffer=io.StringIO()\n    with patch.object(Path,\\\"read_text\\\",read),patch.object(Path,\\\"exists\\\",exists),patch.object(Path,\\\"write_text\\\") as write,redirect_stdout(buffer):\n        b.tally(out)\n    result=json.loads(write.call_args.args[0])\n    print(mode,result[\\\"verdict\\\"],result[\\\"fails\\\"],result[\\\"splits\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"paired identical reasons pass [] []\nsplit invented-cut control inconclusive [] ['X03 K-invented-cut: v41 settled=split [control expects not supported]']\nmissing floor decision inconclusive [] ['K-impossible-floor: the floor defect split']\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"**Send with changes to the reading instructions and tally.** Keep the proposed writer sentence. The main gap is that two readers can agree that $730B is a floor, both endorse $710.4B, and still produce a clean pass. I reproduced that result in memory. No file was edited and no writer was sent.\n\n1. **Wording — the changed clause is consistent, sourced, and general.** Reaffirming a target tells us management still expects it. Taking the target in full requires evidence for the volume needed in the period. A disclosed comparable can supply that evidence if its capacity or units support the scale and timing. D747 also permits a related figure to support a forecast when the writer explains why it favours one band. Neither route makes the entire target automatic. In the other direction, insufficient evidence for full delivery does not justify inventing a discount. D745 and D749 still allow a specific explanation of why the band cannot be settled. The sentence names no company, figure, or required document type. [Writer request:4](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:4) · [Comparable rule:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:5) · [Closing instruction:9](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/judging-v13s.txt:9) · [D745:11515](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11515) · [D747:11582](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11582) · [D749:11645](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11645) · [D750:11673](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:11673)\n\n2. **Serious — measure S with the existing writer request. Tighten what counts as a settled “yes.”** The source describes *planned* spending above $730B. A lower forecast can be coherent if the writer explains the difference. A reader who adopts $730B as a minimum for the same spending cannot use it to endorse $710.4B. The registration catches a floor-versus-guide disagreement. It misses two readers making the **same** mistake. In a read-only replay, I gave both readers the saved approving explanation on each of X05 and X08 and marked the pairs compatible. The tally returned `pass` on the original answers. For both initial reading and adjudication, require the reasons record to identify what supports the decisive premise: on E, what puts the volume in hand for that period when the writer takes the target in full; on S, how the writer’s use of the plan fits its dollar outcome. Agreement on an unsupported premise goes to adjudication. If both final approvals still rest on it, support remains unsettled. This applies the existing rules without adding a second writer change. [E source:10](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/E/user.txt:10) · [X05 reasoning:255](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/reader-packets/X05.md:255) · [S source:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/S/user.txt:29) · [X08 floor reasoning:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/judging-v13s-blind5-2026-11-23/adjudication/X08.claude.json:1) · [Registration:530](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:530) · [Tally:158](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:158)\n\n3. **Minor — correct two tally outcomes.** I reproduced both with the other cases set to pass. A persistent split on the invented-cut control returns `inconclusive`; the registration explicitly says that control **fails** unless it earns a settled “no.” Separately, when one adjudicator omits a required floor decision, the tally returns `inconclusive` as though the adjudicators had disagreed. Keep that reading pending until the missing decision is supplied. An explicit uphold/reject split remains inconclusive. [Registered outcomes:487](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:487) · [Control tally:176](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:176) · [Defect tally:142](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:142) · [Adjudicator instructions:26](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind_adjudicate.py:26)\n\n4. **Verdict — send the $0 test after items 2 and 3.** I rebuilt S, E, and P-v8 in memory. Each matched its D749 case apart from the system text, and all three matched the registered D750 hash. The six fresh writers, two original controls, publication requirement, and two required P-v8 forecasts match council 65’s design. A clean result supports asking Alex to authorize the paid re-send. [Build:32](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind5.py:32) · [D750 hash:14](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/blind6.py:14) · [Pass conditions:480](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:480) · [D750 decision rule:533](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/SMALL-DESIGN.md:533)"}}
